Browser\nCopying Text\nIn a page, i → Copy text\n■\tTo Copy Selected Text\ns to move cursor to the first character to copy \n→ f (Start) → s to specify a range → f \n(End) \n■\tTo Copy All Text in Text Entry Window\ni (All) \nRefreshing Page\nIn a page, i → Refresh\nEntering URL from History\nIn a page, i → Enter URL → i → Insert → \nEnterURL logs → Select URL\n・\n\t Alternatively, press f → Yahoo! → (PC site \nbrowser) → Enter URL → i → Insert → \nEnterURL logs → Select URL.\n・\n Up to ten URL logs appear, the latest first. When \nthe limit is reached, the oldest page is deleted \nautomatically.\nSearching with New Window\nIn a page, i → Manage content → Web search \n→ Enter text\n・\n\t Alternatively, press f → Yahoo! → (PC site \nbrowser) → Web Search → Enter text.\nSearching Text\nIn a page, i → Manage content → Search → \nEnter text to search\n・\n\t Matching words are highlighted. Press u (Prev) / \nf (Next) to view previous or following match. To \nreturn to a page, press i (Cancel).\nMoving to Top/Bottom of Page\nIn a page, i → Manage content → Jump in \npage → Jump to top/Jump to bottom\nSending URL\nIn a page, i → Manage content → Send URL \n→ S! Mail/SMS → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b, P.4-5 SMS b) \nOpening Previously Viewed Page\nIn a page, i → Manage content → History → \nSelect item\n・\n\t Alternatively, press f → Yahoo! → (PC site \nbrowser) → History → Select URL.\n・\n\t Save up to 50 accessed URLs.\n・\n\t To open in a new tab, highlight URL → i → \nOpen new tab.\nSending Access History\nIn a page, i → Manage content → History → \nHighlight URL → i → Send URL → S! Mail/\nSMS → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b, P.4-5 SMS b) \n・\n\t Alternatively, press f → Yahoo! → (PC site \nbrowser) → History → Highlight URL → i → \nSend URL → S! Mail/SMS.\n\n\n5-10\nInternet Services\n5\nDeleting Access History\nIn a page, i → Manage content → History \n■\tTo Delete a History\nHighlight a URL → i → Delete → Selected \n→ Yes\n■\tTo Delete Multiple Histories \ni → Delete → Multiple → Check histories → \nu (Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Histories\ni → Delete → All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\n・\n\t Alternatively, press f → Yahoo! → (PC site \nbrowser) → History → Highlight URL → i → \nDelete.\nUsing Text on Page\nIn a page, move cursor to text → i → Manage \ncontent → Drag → f (OK) \nOr\nIn a page, move cursor to text → f (1 + seconds) \n・\n\t Only if Pointer setting is On, Drag is available \n(fP.5-10).\n■\tTo Copy Text\nHighlight the last character → f (Copy) \n■\tTo Search with Selected Text \nHighlight the last character → i → Copy and \nsearch → f (OK) \n・\n\t Search result will appear with new tab.\n■\tTo Insert Selected Text to Message\nHighlight the last character → i → Send \nmessage → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Save Selected Text to Notepad\nHighlight the last character → i → Save to \nNotepad → f (OK) → u (Save) \nViewing Only Selected Frame\nIn a page, i → Manage content → Frame in\n・\n\t Some pages may be divided into multiple sections. \nSuch a section is referred to as \"Frame\".\n・\n\t To return to normal view, press i → Manage \ncontent → Frame out.\nViewing Page Details\nIn a page, i → Manage content → Details\n■\tTo View Page Information\nPage information\n■\tTo View Server Certificate\nServer Certification\nChanging Font Size\nIn a page, i → Settings → Font size → Select \nan item\nChanging Character Code\nIn a page, i → Settings → Encoding → Select \nan item\n・\n\t If page text appears garbled, changing character \nencoding may solve the problem.\nChanging Scroll Unit\nIn a page, i → Settings → Scroll unit → Select \nan item\nSwitching to Pointer\nIn a page, i → Settings → Pointer settings → \nOn/Off → On or Off\nChanging Pointer Speed\nIn a page, i → Settings → Pointer settings → \nSpeed → Select item\nShow/Play Image/Sound\nIn a page, i → Settings → Downloads\n■\tTo Set Image\nImages → Show images/Do not show\n■\tTo Set Sound\nSounds → Play sounds/Do not play\nSetting Saving Location\nIn a page, i → Settings → Save to → Memory \ncard first/Phone/Always ask\nClearing Cache\nIn a page, i → Settings → Memory manager \n→ Clear cache → Yes\nDeleting Cookies\nIn a page, i → Settings → Memory manager \n→ Delete cookies → Yes\n\n\n5-11\nInternet Services\n5\nDeleting Certificates\nIn a page, i → Settings → Memory manager \n→ Delete certificates → Yes\nSetting Manufacture Number Notification\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → \nManufacture number → On or Off\nSending/Not Sending Referrer Information\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → Send \nreferer → Select an item\n・\n\t Referrer is a link source URL information. It is sent \nto Web server when accessing websites.\nEnabling Cookies\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → Cookies \n→ Select an item\n・\n\t Select Confirm for acceptance confirmation every \ntime before a cookie is saved. \n・\n Cookie automatically saves identification \ninformation of visitors to handset. Cookies contain \nuser information and allow sites to recognize users \nand track preferences.\nEnabling Script\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → Script \n→ Select item\nChecking Root Certificates\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → Root \ncertificates → Select a certificate\n・\n View electronic certificate preinstalled on handset.\nCertificating Retention\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → \nCertificate retention → Select an item\nShowing/Hiding Secure Prompt\nIn a page, i → Settings → Security → Secure \nprompt → On/Off\nInitializing Saved Information\nIn a page, i → Settings → Initialize browser \n→ Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n・\n\t Initialize browser settings or information such as \nBookmarks or Saved pages.\nResetting Yahoo! Keitai/PC Site Browser \nSettings\nIn a page, i → Settings → Reset settings → \nEnter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\nExiting Browser\nIn a page, i → End application → Yes\nYahoo! Keitai\nMoving to Main Menu\nIn a page, i → Yahoo! Keitai\nPC Site Browser\nCapturing Page\nIn a page, i → Capture screen\n・\n\t Save screenshot to