prevent unwanted image blur.\n・\n\t\nDo not expose handset to devices with \nstatic electricity when using camera.\n・\n\t\nCamera employs high precision \ntechnology, however, some pixels may \nseem brighter or darker than others.\n・\n\t\nLeaving handset in a hot place for an \nextended period before capturing/saving \nimage may affect image quality.\n・\n\t\nExposing lens to direct sunlight may \naffect image color.\n・\n\t\nWhen battery is low, camera may be \nunavailable.\nVariety of Capturing Mode\nChoose applicable mode; Multi shot, Scene, etc., \naccording to conditions (fP.6-3).\n\n\n6-3\nCamera & Imaging\n6\nCamera\nFor capturing still images, select Shooting mode: \nNormal to shoot single image and Multi shot or \nPhoto combi to shoot multi-shot.\nCaptured images are saved to Pictures. Insert \nMemory Card to save images to Digital camera.\nUsing Display as Viewfinder\nStill Image Viewfinder\na b c d e f\ng\nh\ni\nj\nk\na\nMode\n : Normal\n : Scene\n : Multi shot\n : Photo combi\n : Video\nScene type\n : Auto\n1\n : Landscape\n1\n : Night\n1\n : Sports\n1\n : Indoor\n1\n : Beach/Snow\n1\n : Sunset\n1\n : Dawn\n1\n : Fall color\n1\n : Firework\n1\n : Text\n1\n : Candlelight\n1\n : Against light\n1\nNumber of capture\n : 6 photos\n1\n : 9 photos\n1\na\nSpeed\n : Fast\n2\n : Normal\n2\n : Slow\n2\n : Manual\n2\nb\nSize\n : 3.1 M (1536x2048) \n3\n : Wide 2.4 M (1232x2048) \n3\n : 2 M (1200x1600) \n3\n : Wide 1.5 M (960x1600) \n3\n : Wide 1.0 M (768x1280) \n3\n : 0.3 M (480x640) \n3\n : Wallpaper (240x400) \n : Mail (240x320) \nc\nMacro\n : On\n : Off\nd\nTimer\n : Off\n\t\n : 3 sec.  \n : 5 sec.\n\t\n : 10 sec.\ne\nWhite Balance\n : Auto\n\t\n : Daylight \n : Incandescent\n\t\n : Fluorescent\n : Cloudy\nf\nBattery level\n\n\n6-4\n6\nCamera & Imaging\ng\nQuality\n : Superfine\n : Fine\n : Normal\nh\nISO\n : Auto\n\t\n : 100\n : 200\n\t\n\t\n : 400\ni\nExposure metering\n：Matrix\n：Center-weight\n：Spot\nj\nNumber of remaining available shots\nk\nSave to\n : Phone\n : Memory card first, Digital\n　　camera first or Always ask\n1\tAppears under Mode or Size.\n2\tAppears under Size or Macro.\n3\tAppears in Normal or Scene Mode.\n・\n\tPress j to show/hide icons and current settings.\nShooting Mode\nDescription\nNormal\nCapture still image and select \nsize by purpose; attach images \nto S! Mail, save as Wallpaper, \netc.\nScene\nSuitable for capturing night \nscenes and landscapes.\nMulti shot\nCapture six or nine images; \nselect auto shutter speed or \nmanual shutter release.\nPhoto combi\nCapture sequential images \nmanually. Select Frame to \nautomatically combine the \nimages into one image.\n\n\nCamera & Imaging\n6-5\n6\nSingle Shot\nPress i\nSet Shooting Mode\n and press u(Done) / c\nSave automatically or\nmanually depending on \nAuto save settings (fP.13-18)\nPress f(           )\n・\n\t Adjusting size and brightness are available for still images.\n・\n\t Attach captured image to message (fP.6-12).\n・\n\t Captured images are saved to Pictures. Insert Memory Card and set save location to Digital Camera folder to save images to Digital camera.\n\n\n6-6\n6\nCamera & Imaging\nNormal\na\tj\n・\n\tAdjust settings before capturing as required \n(fP.6-12).\nb\tFrame image in Viewfinder\n・\n\tFor some sizes, use r to zoom in/out.\n・\n\tUse g to adjust brightness.\nc\tf (\n) \n・\n\tImages are saved automatically.\n・\n\tSet Auto save to Off to save manually \n(fP.13-18).\nScene\na\tj\nb\ti → Scene\nc\tScene type → Select a scene → u \n(Done) / c\n・\n\tAdjust settings before capturing as required \n(fP.6-12).\n・\n\tISO, Exposure metering and Effect are \nunavailable for Scene.\nd\tFrame image in Viewfinder\n・\n\tFor some sizes, use r to zoom in/out.\ne\tf (\n) \n・\n\tImages are saved automatically.\n・\n\tSet Auto save to Off to save manually \n(fP.13-18).\n\nMulti Shot\na\tj\nb\ti → Multi shot\nc\tNumber of capture → Select image \ncount\nd\tSpeed → Fast, Normal, Slow or \nManual → u (Done) / c\n・\n\tAdjust settings before capturing as re