nSave up to ten Alarms. Use Alarm activation to \nactivate or cancel Alarm settings. Set Alarms to \nrepeat on specific days of the week or everyday.\nSetting/Canceling Alarms\nExample: Setting Alarm time\n・\n\t For other items, see \"Editing Alarm\" (fP.9-3).\nSetting\na\tf → Alarm\nb\tSelect Alarm → In Alarm time field, \nenter Alarm time\nc\tu (Save) \n・\n\t\n is shown.\n・\n\tSet or edit Alarm and press u (Save), \nAlarm is set to On automatically.\n・\n\tAt Alarm time, tone sounds and indicator appears. \nHandset vibrates if Vibration is not Off. When Snooze \nis Off, press f (Stop) to stop Alarm and Vibration.\n・\n\tIf calling, dialing (Connecting... appears), or \ndialing (Dialling... appears) at Alarm time, \nan indicator appears. Press f (Stop) to clear \nindicator, when Snooze is Off.\n・\n\tWhen Snooze is set to something other than \nOff, Alarm sounds at the specified interval and \nspecified number of times until Snooze is canceled. \nWhen you press f (Snooze) while Alarm sounds, \nAlarm is set to sound again at the specified \ninterval. Press i (End) → End to stop Alarm and \nto clear indicator.\n・\n If multiple Alarms are set for the same time, first \nset sounds first. If Schedule or Tasks Alarm is set \nfor the same time as Alarm (Tools), Alarm sounds \nfirst.\n・\n\tWhen Manner mode is active, setting in Manner \nmode setting (fP.9-17) applies.\n・\n\tIf Camera or Voice Recorder is active at Alarm \nTime, Alarm sounds upon operation termination.\nCanceling Alarm\na\tf → Alarm → Highlight Alarm → \nu (On/Off) \nEditing Alarm\na\tf → Alarm → Select Alarm\n■\t To Set Alarm Time\nHighlight Alarm Time → Enter Alarm time → \nu (Save) \n■\t To Set Alarm to Repeat\nRepeat → Select item → u (Save) \n・\n\tIf Selected day is selected, check day → \nu (Done).\n・\n\tIf you set Alarm for every day, Alarm will \nactivate daily.\n■\t To Activate/Cancel Alarm for Holidays\nExcept holidays → On or Off → u \n(Save) \n■\t To Set Snooze\nSnooze → Select an item → u (Save) \n・\n\tWhen Snooze is set to something other \nthan Off, Alarm sounds at the specified \ninterval and specified number of times \nuntil Snooze is canceled. When you press \nf (Snooze) while Alarm sounds, Alarm \nis set to sound again at the specified \ninterval. Press i (End) → End to stop \nAlarm and to clear indicator.\n・\n\tFor Other, enter minutes.\n■\t To Set Snooze Repeat Time (s) \nSnooze repeat times → Select an item → \nu (Save) \n■\t To Set Alarm Sound/Sound Video\nAlarm tone/video → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → u (Save) \n・\n In list, press u (Play) to play file.\n\n\n9-4\n9\nHandy Extras\n■\t To Adjust Alarm Volume\nVolume → Adjust volume → u (Save) \n・\n\tPress u (play) to play file.\n■\t To Set Vibration\nVibration → Select an item → u (Save) \n・\n\tPress u (play) to view a pattern.\n■\t To Set Alarm Duration Time\nDuration → Select an item → u (Save) \n・\n\tFor Other, enter duration.\n■\t To Edit Alarm Name\nAlarm name → Enter Alarm name → u \n(Save) \n・\n \nIf a Memory Card file is set as Alarm sound, copy \nto handset confirmation appears. For a copy \nprotected file, move to handset confirmation \nappears. Choose Yes to complete setting.\nAdvanced\nb rP.9-16\n●\n●Resetting Alarm\n●\n●Setting Alarm Sound/Vibration in Manner Mode\nCalendar\nTo view Calendar, add schedule in Calendar.\nSelect from three view modes.\nAdd Title, Start date or other information.\nSave up to 500 events including Tasks.\nViewing Calendar\nSelect from three view modes; Monthly view, Weekly \nview and Daily view.\n・\n\t f → Calendar → i → View mode → \nMonth/Week/Day to change view mode.\n・\n\t If you select a date with Calendar entries, the \nentries appear as per the following.\nBlack: Monday to Friday\nBlue: Saturday\nRed: Sunday/Holiday \nDates in black rectangle: Highlighted position\nDay with gray background: Today\n : Schedule registered\nMonthly View\nWeekly View\nDaily View\n・\n\tTo change Monthly/Weekly/Daily view window for \nprevious/next month/week/day, press * / #.\n・\n\tIf you select a date with Calendar entries or Alarms \nset, the titles of Calendar entries, icons and other \nitems appear.\n \n : Schedule (No category) \n \n : Schedule (Appointment) \n \n : Schedule (Meeting) \n \n : Schedule (Business) \n \n : Schedule (Personal) \n \n : Schedule (Holiday) \n \n : Schedule (Anniversary) \n \n : Schedule (Birthday) \n \n : Schedule (Phone call) \n \n : Schedule (Date) \n \n : Schedule (Travel) \n \n : Schedule (Shopping) \n \n : Schedule (Miscellaneous) \n \n : Alarm set\n \n : Repetition set\n\n\n9-5\n9\nHandy Extras\nOpening Calendar\na\tf → Calendar\nSaving Schedule\nSave up to 500 events including Tasks.\nExample: Saving title, start date & time, end date & time.\n・\n\t For other items, see \"Saving to Schedule\" (fP.9-16).\na\tf → Calendar\nb\tu (Add new) \nc\tEnter title\nd\tSelect date & time → In Start date \nfield, enter start date → In Start \ntime field, enter start time\ne\tIn End date field, enter end date \n→ In End time field, enter end time \n→ f (OK) \nf\tu (Save) \n・\n\tIn Calendar, select date before b to enter the \ndate in Start date or End date field.\nViewing Schedule\na\tf → Calendar\nb\tSelect the day to view\nc\tSelect a schedule\n・\n\tTo view the registered number of Schedule and \nTask in Calendar, press i → Memory status.\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-16\n●\n●Switching View Mode\n●\n●Opening a Specific Date\n●\n●Viewing All Events\n●\n●Viewing Schedule by Category\n●\n●Sending Schedule\n●\n●Viewing Secret Schedule\n●\n●Checking Missed Alarm Event\n●\n●Viewing Calendar Memory Status\n●\n●Deleting Schedule\n●\n●Sending Selected Schedule\n●\n●Sending Schedule to Guests\n●\n●Saving Schedule\n\n\n9-6\n9\nHandy Extras\nTasks\nSave up to 500 Schedule entries; manage with \nlists.\nSaving Tasks\nExample: Saving title, due date & time\n・\n\t For other items, see \"Saving Task\" (fP.9-19).\na\tf → Tools → Tasks\nb\tu (Add new) \nc\tEnter a title\nd\tDue date & time → In Due date \nfield, enter due date → In Due time \nfield, enter due time → f (OK) \ne\tu (Save) \nViewing Tasks\na\tf → Tools → Tasks\n・\n\tAlternatively, f → Calendar → Select date → \nTasks.\n・\n\tIn Tasks, press g to toggle \n (All tasks), \n (Completed tasks), \n (Uncompleted \ntasks), and \n (Expired tasks).\nMarking a Task as Completed\na\tf → Tools → Tasks\nb\tHighlight uncompleted task/\nexpired task → i → Status → \nCompleted\n・\n\tHighlight completed tasks → i → Status \n→ Uncompleted tasks to toggle tasks \nbefore due date as \n (Uncompleted) and \ntasks after due date as \n (Expired).\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-18\n●\n●Sending Tasks\n●\n●Sorting Tasks\n●\n●Searching Tasks\n●\n●Saving Tasks\n●\n●Setting Alarm Sound/Vibration in Manner Mode\n●\n●Viewing Secret Tasks\n●\n●Viewing Missed Alarm Event\n●\n●Viewing Task Item Status\n●\n●Deleting Tasks\nStopwatch\nUse handset as a stopwatch. Save up to ten lap \ntimes and total elapsed time.\na\tf → Tools → Stopwatch\nb\tf (Start) \n・\n\tPress u (Lap) to mark a lap.\nLast ten laps are saved.\nc\tf (Stop) \n・\n\tPress i (Save) → Yes to save stopwatch content \nto notepad.\n・\n\tPress f (Restart) to start Stopwatch again.\n・\n\tPress u (Reset) to clear all times.\n\n\n9-7\n9\nHandy Extras\nCountdown Timer\nCount down up to 60 minutes.\na\tf → Tools → Countdown timer\nb\tEnter countdown time\nc\tf (Start) \n・\n\tTo stop counts, press f (Stop).\n・\n\tPress f (Restart) to restart countdown.\n・\n\tPress u (Reset) to reset Countdown Timer.\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-20\n●\n●Changing Alarm\nWorld Clock\nSee current time in world's major cities.\nViewing World Clock\na\tf → Tools → World clock\nSelecting Areas\nSet second time zone to show time in World clock.\na\tf → Tools → World clock\n・Alternatively, press f → Settings \n→ Display settings → Clock/Calendar \n→ Dual clock\nb\tg to select time zone\n・\n\tPress r to select First clock field or \nSecond clock field.\n・\n\tTo set/cancel summer time setting, press \ni (DST).\nc\tf (Save) \nGood Night Timer\nDisable Alarm/Vibration/Light for a specific period \nof time.\n・\n\tWhen Good night timer is On, Alarm/Vibration/\nLight is set to Off, and volume level is set to 0 \nfor functions that use sound.\n・\n\tEven when Good night timer is On, other \nfunctions such as Voice Call, etc. are available.\nSetting Good Night Timer\nNote\n・\n\t\nDeactivate other functions before Good \nnight timer activates. If any other function \nis activated, Good night timer cannot be \nactivated.\na\tf → Tools → Good night timer\nb\tTimer\nc\tIn Start time field, enter start time \n→ In End time field, enter end time\n・\n\tCheck Activate now to start timer after \nGood night timer is set.\nd\tf (OK) \ne\tRepeat → Select an item\n・\n\tCheck Every day to repeat Alarm \neveryday.\n・\n\tIf Activate now is selected in c, setting \nin Repeat will be canceled.\n\n\n9-8\n9\nHandy Extras\nf\tAlarm sounds → On to activate \nAlarm with Alarm tone\ng\tu (Save) \n・\n\tGood night timer will be On automatically.\nCanceling Good Night Timer\na\tf → Tools → Good night timer\nb\tu (On/Off) \nCalculator\nPerform four math operations of up to 13 digits.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Calculator\nb\tEnter numbers and operators\n・\n\tTo add calculation result to notepad, press \ni → Save to Notepad → Yes. Complete \ncalculation to save results to Notepad.\n・\n\tTo exit calculator, press i → End.\n・\n\tTo erase a symbol in a mathematical expression, \npress c.\n・\n\tTo erase mathematical expression and result all at \nonce, press u (AC).\nNotepad\nAdd up to 100 memos. Add memos even while \nplacing calls (fP.3-18).\nAdding Notepad\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Notepad\nb\tu (Add) → Enter text\nc\tSelect category field → Select \ncategory\nd\tu (Save) \nViewing Notepad\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Notepad \n→ Select Notepad\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-20\n●\n●Searching Notepad\n●\n●Viewing Notes by Category\n●\n●Sending Notepad\n●\n●Saving Notes to Data Folder\n●\n●Viewing Notepad Memory Status\n●\n●Deleting Notepad\n\n\n9-9\n9\nHandy Extras\nBarcode/Scan\nUse Camera to scan printed barcodes, QR Codes, \nname cards, text, or keywords. Use scanned \nbarcodes to acquire images from websites, etc.\nScanning Barcode/QR Code/Name Card/\nText/Keyword\nNote\n・\n\t\nIf text is too small to scan or is not focused \non, scanned result may be incorrect.\n・\n\t\nSome barcodes/text may be invalid.\n・\n\t\nScan may fail if barcode/text is not clear.\n・\n\t\nIndoors, scan may fail if handset shadows \nbarcode/text.\n・\n\t\nHold handset approximately 10 cm away \nfrom barcode/text. If it does not scan, move \nhandset slowly to adjust the distance to fix \nfocus.\n・\n\tPress u (Macro) to set/cancel Macro.\n・\n To adjust brightness, use g.\nBarcodes/QR Codes\nBarcode Reader automatically identifies and scans \nBarcodes (JAN code) and QR Codes. Use scan results \nfor handset operations such as calling.\nQR Code\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Scan barcode\nb\tUse Display to frame barcode → \nf (Scan) \n・\n\tCamera focuses on and scans barcode \nautomatically.\n・\n\tScan may fail when capturing multiple barcodes.\n・\n\tJAN codes are one-dimensional codes made up of \ncombinations of vertical bars of varying widths and \nspaces. Handset is not compatible with other 1D \ncodes (e.g., ITF code, Code39, or Codebar/NW-7).\n・\n\tQR Code is two-dimensional code with information \nin matrix.\n・\n\tTo save scanned result, u (Save).\n To view saved barcode, in Scan barcode window, \npress i → Scan results.\n・\n\tTo scan multiple barcodes continuously, activate \nBarcode code reader → i → Continues scan. \nAfter a scan is complete, choose Yes to scan the \nnext barcode.\n・\n\tSplit barcodes cannot be opened or saved unless \nall split barcodes are scanned.\n・\n\tYou can use any phone numbers, mail addresses, \nor other items for Phone Book entries if they are \ncontained in the scanned data (fP.9-21). For usable \ninformation, the background color of the text turns \ntheme color; however, if the text contains any \ncharacter that is not allowed to be used for that \ninformation, the background area for the following \ncharacters does not change into theme color.\n・\n\tUse QR Codes for text only. Handset cannot scan \nQR Codes created from media files.\n\n\n9-10\n9\nHandy Extras\nName Card\nScan name card and save to Phone Book, etc.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Name card reader\nb\tUse Display to frame name card → \nf (Scan) \n・\n\tCamera focuses on and scans name card \nautomatically.\n・\n\tTo save the scanned result, press f (Register) → \nu (Save).\nText\nScan text and save/edit it.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Text reader\nb\tUse Display to frame text → f \n(Scan) \n・\n\tCamera focuses on and scans text \nautomatically.\n・\n\tPress r to adjust scanning range.\n・\n\tTo save the scanned result, press f (OK) → u \n(Save). To check the saved text, press i → Scan \nresults.\n・\n\tTo edit the scanned result, edit after scanning.\n・\n\tTo toggle recognition language, press i → \nLanguage → Automatic/Japanese/English.\nScanning a Keyword & Looking It up in \nDictionary\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Dictionary reader\nb\tUse Display to frame word \n→ f (Scan) \n・\n\tCamera focuses on and scans text \nautomatically.\nc\tSelect scanned result\n・\n\tTo toggle dictionary, press i (Switch) → \nEnglish/Japanese.\nUsing Barcode Files\nUse a barcode file saved in Data Folder.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Open barcode → Select \nfolder\n・\n\tWith Memory Card inserted, select a file \nfrom Pictures or Digital Camera folder.\nb\tSelect a file\n・\n\tCamera focuses on and scans text \nautomatically.\n・\n\tFor split barcodes, once one portion is scanned, \nthe rest is automatically recognized and scanned. \nIf file name or saved directory of a split barcode \nhas been changed, select unrecognized part to be \nscanned.\n・\n If file has been altered, barcode may not scan.\n・\n If barcode is unrecognizable, notification appears.\n\n\n9-11\n9\nHandy Extras\nCreating QR Code\nUse Phone Book entry or enter text to create QR \nCode.\n・\n\tA QR Code holds up to 211 single-byte or 105 \ndouble-byte characters.\n・\n When volume of information is large, a split \nQR Code automatically appears (up to 16 QR \nCodes).\n・\n\tCreated QR Code is saved in Pictures in Data \nFolder. Check saved QR Code in Data Folder \n(fP.9-10).\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Create QR code\nb\tCreate QR Code\n■\t To Create QR Code from Phone Book \nEntry\nPhonebook → Search and select entry \n(fP.2-13) → Select a phone number\n■\t To Enter Account Details\nMy details\n■\t To Create Text QR Code\nText input → Enter text\nc\tf (Save) \n・\n \t\nTo specify saving location for created QR \nCode, press i → Save to → Select an \nitem → f (Save).\n・\n\tPhone Book entries converted to QR Codes \ncontain Name, Reading name, Phone number, Mail \naddress, Address, and Memo. Other items will not \nbe included.\n・\n\tPress u (Send) in QR Code confirmation window \nto create S! Mail with the created QR Code \nattached.\nChecking Scanned Barcode/Text\nCheck the saved scanned result.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/\nScan → Scan results\nb\tSelect a result\n・\n\tIf scanned result is too large, it will not appear. \nSome files cannot be opened.\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-21\n●\n●Renaming Scanned Data\n●\n●Viewing Scanned Data Detail\n●\n●Deleting Scanned Data\n\n\n9-12\n9\nHandy Extras\nConverter\nConvert various currencies or units of \nmeasurement.\nConverting Currencies\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Converter \n→ Currency\nb\tSelect Original currency field → \nSelect currency\nc\tIn Original currency value field, \nenter value\nd\tSee result in Converted currency \nvalue field\n・\n\tTo save results to notepad, press i → \nSave to Notepad → Yes.\n・\n\tTo exit converter, press i → End.\nConverting Units\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Converter \n→ Length, Weight, Volume, Area, \nor Temperature\nb\tSelect Original unit field \n→ Select unit\nc\tIn Original unit value field, enter \nvalue\nd\tSee result in Converted value field\n・\n\tTo save results to notepad, press i → \nSave to Notepad → Yes.\n・\n\tTo exit converter, press i → End.\nSplit the Bill\nDivide Total Cost with two different ratios.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Split the \nbill\nb\tIn Total Cost field, enter price\nc\tIn Number of people A field, enter \nnumber\nd\tIn Number of people B field, enter \nnumber\ne\tg to charge ratio\n・\n\tCost and amount of carry-over for A and B \nare shown.\n・\n\tIn Split the Bill window, press i (Settings) → \nPayment unit → Select an item → c.\n・\n\tTo change method of collecting extra changes, \nin Split the Bill window, press i (Settings) → \nCollect extra fee → On/Off → c.\n\n\n9-13\n9\nHandy Extras\nVoice Recorder\nRecord up to 60 minutes; activate from Tools, or \nvia Menu in Data Folder, or during a call, Message \ncreation window.\nVoice Recorder Window\nUse Softkeys and Multi Selector operations to control \nVoice Recorder.\nRecording Window\nPlayback Window\na\nb\nc\nd\na\tStatus bar\nb\tRecordable time (while recording)/\nPlayback time (while playing) \nc\tElapsed time\nd\tVolume\nRecording Sound\nRecorded sound is saved to Ring Songs・Tones in \nData Folder.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Voice \nrecorder\nb\tf (Record) \nc\tu (Stop) \n・\n\tAfter recording, files are saved automatically \nto Ring Songs・Tones under Data Folder.\n・\n\tWhen recordable time has elapsed, \nrecording automatically ends.\n・\n\tAfter pressing f (Pause), press u (Save) \nto save file.\n・\n\tPress f (Pause) to pause recording. Press \nf (Record) to resume recording.\n・\n To quickly confirm recorded content, press f (Play). \nPress f (Pause) again to pause playback.\n・\n\tTo start the next recording, press i → Record.\nPlaying Sound\nPlay sound file saved in Data Folder.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Voice \nrecorder\nb\ti → Data folder\nc\tSelect a sound file\n・\n\tUse r to adjust volume.\n・\n\tUse g to rewind/fast forward.\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-22\n●\n●Moving Recorded Sound File\n●\n●Copying Recorded Sound File\n●\n●Sending Recorded Sound File\n●\n●Editing Recorded Sound File Name\n●\n●Viewing Recorded Sound File Details\n●\n●Deleting Recorded Sound File\n\n\n9-14\n9\nHandy Extras\nFile Viewer\nView document files in Standard view or \nFullscreen. Rotate Display image using menu.\n・\n\tThis guide describes standard view operations. \nStandard View\n       \nFullscreen View\nNote\n・\n\t\nIf a document includes many pages or \ncomplicated designs, all pages of the \ndocument may not appear properly.\n・\n\t\nTo view file containing Japanese/English/\nHangul/Chinese (simplified characters)/\nPortuguese properly, set the language.\nUsing File Viewer\na\tf → Tools → Useful → File \nviewer\nb\tSelect a file\nc\tScroll the file\n・\n Use r to flip page.\n・\n Open PDF, XLS, DOC, PPT, or TXT files saved in \nData Folder. Select an image file saved in Data \nFolder and File viewer is activated automatically.\n・\n\tFiles with up to approximately 4 MB can be \nbrowsed. However, browse files of up to 4 MB. \nIn some cases, files under 4 MB may not be \nbrowsable.\nZooming In/Out\na\tf → Tools → Useful → File \nviewer → Select a file\nb\ti → Zoom → In/Out\n・\n\tAlternatively, press i / u to adjust \nmagnification.\n・\n\tPress i → Fit to screen → Page/Width/\nHeight to change Display view.\n\n\n9-15\n9\nHandy Extras\nAdvanced\nbrP.9-23\n●\n●Deleting Files\n●\n●Toggling Standard View/Fullscreen View\n●\n●Searching Characters in Page\n●\n●Going to Pages\n●\n●Rotating Display Image\n●\n●Capturing Images\n●\n●Sending Files\n●\n●Editing File Name\n●\n●Protecting File\n●\n●Viewing File Details\n●\n●Viewing Shortcut Key\nMagnifier\nUse Magnifier to view small characters or distant \nscenery.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Magnifier\n・\n\tPress u (Macro) to set Macro.\n・\n\tTo adjust brightness, press g.\n・\n\tTo adjust zoom, press r.\n・\n\tAlternatively, press f → Camera → Magnifier.\nDictionary\nLook up words in English/Japanese dictionaries.\na\tf → Tools → Useful → Dictionary\nb\tEnglish dictionary or Japanese \ndictionary\nc\tEnter a word\nd\tSelect a word\n・\n\tTo save search data to notepad, press u \n(Save) → Yes.\n・Press u (Switch) to toggle English \ndictionary/Japanese dictionary.\n\n\n9-16\n9\nHandy Extras\nAdvanced Settings\nAlarm\nResetting Alarm\nf → Alarm\n■\tTo Reset an Alarm\nHighlight alarm → i → Reset → Selected → \nYes\n■\tTo Reset Multiple Alarms\ni → Reset → Multiple → Check alarms → \nu (Reset) → Yes\n■\tTo Reset All Alarms\ni → Reset → All → Yes\nSetting Alarm Sound/Vibration in Manner Mode\nf → Alarm → i → Manner mode setting → \nAlarm sound/Vibration → On or Off\nCalendar\nAdding Schedule Quickly\nf → Calendar → u (Hold: Quick) → Enter title \n→ Select date → In Start date field, enter start date \n→ In Start time field, enter start time → In End \ndate field, enter end date → In End time field, enter \nend time → f (OK) \n・\n\t To set schedule for all day, check All day → f \n(OK).\nSaving to Schedule\nf → Calendar → u (Add new) \n→ Enter title → Select date & time → In Start date \nfield, enter start date → In Start time field, enter \nstart time → In End date field, enter end date → In \nEnd time field, enter end time → f (OK) \n■\tTo Set Schedule for All Day\nSelect date & time → Check All day → f (OK) \n→ u (Save) \n■\tTo Set Category\nCategory → Select an item → u (Save) \n■\tTo Set Alarm\nAlarm → Alarm time → Select an item \n→ Duration → Select an item → Alarm tone/\nvideo → Select a file location → Select a file \n→ Volume → Adjust Volume → Vibration \n→ Select an item → u (Done) → u (Save) \n・\n\t For Other in Alarm time or Duration, enter \nAlarm time or duration.\n・\n\t While selecting Alarm tone/video, press u \n(Play) to playback a file.\n・\n\t While selecting Vibration, press u (Play) to \nview a pattern.\n・\n\t If a Memory Card file is set as Alarm sound, copy to \nhandset confirmation appears. For a copy protected \nfile, move to handset confirmation appears.\n■ To Repeat a Set Schedule\nRepeat → Select an item → Enter a number of \ntimes to repeat → f (OK) → u (Save) \n・\n\t If No repetition is selected, you do not need to \nenter the number of times to repeat.\n・\n\t At Alarm time, tone sounds and indicator \nappears. Press f (Stop) to stop Alarm and \nindicator is cleared. If no Alarm is stopped, \nMissed Alarm message appears. Select the \nmessage to view the event.\n・\n\t During a call, while dialing (Connecting... \nappears) or while dialing (Dialling... appears), \nat Alarm time, an indicator appears. Press f \n(Stop) to clear indicator.\n■\tTo Set Location\nLocation → Enter location → u (Save) \n■\tTo Set Guests\nGuests → From phonebook/Enter number/\nEnter address → Search and select phone \nnumber (fP.2-13)/Enter number/Enter address → \nu (OK) → u (Save) \n・\n\t Press i → Add to add guests.\n・\n\t To remove guest, perform following operations.\n-\t To Remove a Guest\nHighlight a guest → i → Remove → \nSelected\n-\t To Remove Multiple Guests\ni → Remove → Multiple → Check guests \n→ u (Remove) \n-\t To Remove All Guests\ni → Remove → All\n■\tTo Automatically Delete Schedule\nExpiry → Select an item → u (Save) \n・\n\t Upon expiry, schedule is automatically deleted \nfrom Calendar (e.g. if Expiry is After 1 year, \nand Repetition is unset, schedule is deleted one \nyear from event end date). If Repetition is set, \nschedule is deleted one year after last repetition. \nSelect Off to cancel Auto delete.\n\n\n9-17\n9\nHandy Extras\n■\tTo Set Schedule in Detail\nDetails → Enter text → u (Save) \n■\tTo Set Secret\nSecret → On or Off → u (Save) \nEditing Schedule\nf → Calendar → Select date → Select schedule \n→ f (Edit) → Edit and save to Schedule (fP.9-16) \nSwitching View Mode\nf → Calendar → i → View mode → Month/\nWeek/Day\nOpening a Specific Date\nf → Calendar → i → Go to\n■\tTo Show Today's Date\nToday\n■\tTo Toggle to a Specified Date\nDate → Enter date\nViewing All Events\nf → Calendar → i → Show all events\nViewing Schedule by Category\nf → Calendar → i → List by category → \nSelect item\nSending Schedule\nf → Calendar → i → Send via infrared → \nCheck Schedule → u (Send) (fP.12-3) \nSetting Holiday\nf → Calendar → i → Settings → Set \nholiday → (if holiday is already added, i → Add \n→ ) Enter title → u (Save) \n・\n\t To change date, highlight Date → Enter date.\n・\n\t To change frequency, Frequency → Select an \nitem.\nChanging Holiday Display\nf → Calendar → i → Settings → Set \nholiday → u (On/Off) \nEditing Added Holiday\nf → Calendar → i → Settings → Set \nholiday → Select holiday → Edit the entry → \nu (Save) \nDeleting Added Holiday\nf → Calendar → i → Settings → Set \nholiday → Highlight holiday → i → Delete\nSetting Beginning of Week\nf → Calendar → i → Settings → Starting \nday → Sunday or Monday\nSetting Default Calendar View\nf → Calendar → i → Settings \n→ Default view mode → Select an item\nSetting Alarm Sound/Vibration in Manner Mode\nf → Calendar → i → Settings → Manner \nmode setting → Alarm sound/Vibration → On \nor Off\nViewing Secret Schedule\nf → Calendar → i → Unlock temporarily \n→ Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \nChecking Missed Alarm Event\nf → Calendar → i → Missed alarm event \n→ Select a schedule\nViewing Calendar Memory Status\nf → Calendar → i → Memory status\n・\n\t To delete schedule, highlight item → u (Delete) \n→ Yes → Check items → u (Delete) → Yes.\nDeleting Schedule\nf → Calendar\n■\tTo Delete an Entry\nSelect a date in Monthly view or Weekly view → \nHighlight schedule → i → Delete → Selected \n→ Yes\n■\tTo Delete Schedules for Selected Date\nSelect a date in Monthly view or Weekly view \n→ i → Delete \n・\n\t To Delete Multiple Schedules\nMultiple → Check schedules → u (Delete) \n→ Yes\n・\n\t To Delete All the Schedules\nAll → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \n→ Yes\n\n\n9-18\n9\nHandy Extras\n・\n\t Alternatively, in Monthly view/Weekly view → \nHighlight date → i → Delete → All this \nday → Yes.\n■\tTo Delete Schedules for a Specified Period of \nTime\nIn Monthly view or Weekly view, i → Delete \n→ Periods → In From field, enter start date → \nIn To field, enter end date → f (Delete) \n→ Yes\n■\tTo Delete Schedules of Currently Shown \nMonth/Week\nIn Monthly view or Weekly view, i → Delete \n→ This month or This week → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Schedules before the \nHighlighted Date\nIn Monthly view or Weekly view, i → Delete \n→ All past data → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Schedules\nIn the Monthly view or Weekly view, i \n→ Delete → All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete Multiple Schedules Listed by \nCategory\nIn Monthly view or Weekly view, i → List by \ncategory → Select a category\n・\n\t To Delete Multiple Schedules\ni → Delete → Multiple → Check schedules \n→ u (Delete) → Yes\n・\n\t To Delete All the Schedules in Category\ni → Delete → All (This category) → Yes\n・\n\t To Delete All the Schedules in All Categories\ni → Delete → All (All categories) → \nEnter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete from Daily View\n・\n\t To Delete A Schedule\nIn Daily view, highlight schedule → i → \nDelete → Selected → Yes\n・\n\t To Delete Multiple Schedules\nIn Daily view → i → Delete → Multiple → \nCheck Schedule → u (Delete) → Yes\n・\n\t To Delete All the Schedules\nIn Daily view → i → Delete → All → Enter \nPhone Password → f (OK) → Yes\nSending Selected Schedule\nf → Calendar → Select date → Highlight \nschedule → i → Send\n■\tTo Send via Message\nVia message → Check schedules → u (Send) \n→ (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Send via Infrared\nVia infrared → Check schedules → u (Send) \n(fP.12-3) \n・\n\t Alternatively, in Detailed information window, \npress i → Send to send it.\nSending Schedule to Guests\nf → Calendar → Select date → Highlight \nschedule → i → Send invitation → u (Send) \n・\n Alternatively, in Detailed information window, \npress i → Send invitation.\nSaving Schedule\nf → Calendar → Select date → highlight \nschedule → i → Save to Data Folder → \nPhone/Memory card → Yes\n・\n\t Alternatively, in Detailed information window, press \ni → Save to Data Folder → Phone/Memory \ncard → Yes.\n・\n\t Save location can be set to Memory card if \ninserted.\nTasks\nSaving Task\nf → Tools → Tasks → u (Add new) → Enter \ntitle → Due date & time → In Due date field, \nenter due date → In Due time field, enter due time \n→ f (OK) \n■\tTo Set Alarm\nAlarm → Alarm time → Select an item → \nDuration → Select an item → Alert tone/\nvideo → Select a file location → Select a file \n→ Volume → Adjust volume → Vibration → \nSelect an item → u (Done) → u (Save) \n・\n\t If Other is selected in Alarm time/Duration, \nenter alarm date and time/duration.\n・\n\t While selecting Alert tone/video, press u \n(Play) to playback a file.\n・\n\t While selecting Vibration, press u (Play) to \nview a pattern.\n\n\n9-19\n9\nHandy Extras\n・\n If a Memory Card file is set as Alarm sound, copy \nto handset confirmation appears. For a copy \nprotected file, move to handset confirmation \nappears. Choose Yes to complete setting.\n・\n\t At Alarm time, tone sounds and indicator \nappears. Press f (Stop) to stop Alarm and \nindicator is cleared. If no Alarm is stopped, \nMissed Alarm message appears. Select the \nmessage to view the event.\n・\n\t During a call, while dialing (Connecting... \nappears) or while dialing (Dialling... appears), \nat Alarm time, an indicator appears. Press f \n(Stop) to clear indicator.\n■\tTo Set Priority\nPriority → Select an item → u (Save) \n■\tTo Set Details\nDetails → Enter content → u (Save) \n■\tTo Activate/Cancel Secret\nSecret → On or Off → u (Save) \nEditing Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks → Select a task → f (Edit) \n→ Edit Task (fP.9-18) \nSending Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Send\n■\tTo Send via Message\nVia message → Check tasks → u (Send) \n→ (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Send via Infrared\nVia infrared → Check tasks → u (Send) \n→ (fP.12-3) \n・\n\t Alternatively, in Task details window, press u → \nSend.\nSorting Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Sort by \n→ Deadline or Priority\nSearching Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Search → By \ndue date/By title → Enter Expiration/Title\nSaving Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks → Select a task → i → \nSave to Data Folder → Phone/Memory card \n→ Yes\n・\n\t Alternatively, in list, press i → Save to Data \nFolder → Phone/Memory card → Yes.\n・\n\t With Memory Card inserted, Memory card can be \nset as save location.\nSetting Alarm Sound/Vibration in Manner Mode\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Manner mode \nsetting → Alarm sound/Vibration → On or Off\nViewing Secret Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Unlock \ntemporarily → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \nViewing Missed Alarm Event\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Missed alarm \nevent → Select a missed task\nViewing Task Item Status\nf → Tools → Tasks → i → Memory status\n・\n\t To delete tasks, highlight item → u (Delete) → \nYes → Select item → u (Delete) → Yes.\nDeleting Tasks\nf → Tools → Tasks\n■\tTo Delete a Task\nHighlight task → i → Delete → Selected → \nYes\n・\n\t Alternatively, in Detailed information window, \npress i → Delete → Yes.\n■\tTo Select a Tab & Delete\nHighlight Completed tasks/Uncompleted \ntasks/Expired tasks tab → i → Delete\n・\n\t To Delete a Task\nSelected → Yes\n・\n\t To Delete Multiple Tasks\nMultiple → Check tasks → u (Delete) → \nYes\n・\n\t To Delete All the Tasks in a Tab\nAll this tab → Yes\n■\tTo Delete Multiple Tasks\ni → Delete → Multiple → Check tasks → \nu (Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Tasks\ni → Delete → All tasks → Enter Phone \nPassword → f (OK) → Yes\n・\n\t Alternatively, highlight Completed tasks/\nUncompleted tasks/Expired tasks tab → i → \nDelete → All tasks → Enter Phone Password → \nf (OK) → Yes.\n\n\n9-20\n9\nHandy Extras\nCountdown Timer\nChanging Alarm\nf → Tools → Countdown timer → i \n(Settings) \n■\tTo Set Duration\nDuration → Select item\n・\n\t When selecting Other, enter duration time.\n■\tTo Set Alert Tone\nSounds/Alerts → Select a file location → Select \nfile \n・\n While selecting file, press u (Play) to check the \nsound.\n・\n If a Memory Card file is set to alarm, copy \nto handset confirmation appears. For a copy \nprotected file, move to handset confirmation \nappears. Select Yes to complete settings.\n■\tTo Set Volume\nVolume → Adjust volume\n■\tTo Set Vibration\nVibration → Select item\n・\n\t While selecting a Vibration pattern, press u \n(Play) to check the pattern.\nGood Night Timer\nResetting Good Night Timer\nf → Tools → Good night timer → i (Reset) → \nYes\nNotepad\nChanging Notepad Category\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → Select a \nNotepad → Select Category field → Select category\nEditing Notepad\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → Select a \nNotepad → Select Edit memo field → Edit Notepad\nSearching Notepad\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → i → \nSearch → Enter search text\nViewing Notes by Category\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → i → List \nby category → Select category\nSending Notepad\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → i → \nSend\n■\tTo Use Notepad Data as Message Text\nAs message text → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n・\n\t If Notepad contains Hangul characters, Graphic \nMail and Auto art will be unavailable. \n■\tTo Send via Message\nVia message → Check Notepads → u (Send) \n→ (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Send via Infrared\nVia infrared → Check Notepads → u (Send) \n→ (fP.12-3) \n・\n\t Press u (Send) in Details window to send.\nSaving Notes to Data Folder\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → Highlight \nNotepad → i → Save to Data Folder → \nPhone/Memory card → Yes\n・\n\t Alternatively, in Details window, press i → Save \nto Data Folder → Phone/Memory card → \nYes.\n・\n\t With Memory Card inserted, Memory Card is \nselectable.\nViewing Notepad Memory Status\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad → i → \nMemory status\n・\n\t To delete notepad, highlight item → u (Delete) \n→ Yes → Check item → u (Delete) → Yes.\nDeleting Notepad\nf → Tools → Useful → Notepad\n■\tTo Delete a Notepad\nHighlight a Notepad → i → Delete → Selected \n→ Yes\n・\n\t Alternatively, in Details window, press i → \nDelete → Yes.\n■\tTo Delete Multiple Notepads\ni → Delete → Multiple → Check Notepads \n→ u (Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Notepads\ni → Delete → All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\n\n\n9-21\n9\nHandy Extras\nBarcode/Scan\nUsing Scanned Data\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nScan barcode → Scan a barcode\n■\tTo Call Scanned Phone Number\nHighlight a number with TEL: or ten to 32-digit \nnumber starting with 0 → f (Select) → \nVoice call or Edit before call\n・\n\t If Edit before call is selected, edit phone \nnumber then press t / f (\n).\n■\tTo Send Message to Scanned Phone Number\nHighlight a number with TEL: or ten to 32-digit \nnumber starting with 0 → f (Select) → Create \nmessage → S! Mail or SMS (fP.4-4 S! Mail e, \nfP.4-5 SMS e) \n■\tTo Send Message to Scanned Mail Address\nHighlight mail address contained with @ → f \n(Select) → Create message → (fP.4-4 S! Mail \ne) \n■\tTo Access Scanned URL\nHighlight URL starting with http: // → f \n(Select) → Open Yahoo! Keitai/Open PC site \nbrowser → Yes \n■\tTo Save Scanned Entry to Phone Book\nHighlight an entry → f (Select) → u (Save) \n■\tTo Save Scanned Number, etc. as a New \nPhone Book Entry\nHighlight a phone number, etc. → f (Select) \n→ Add to phonebook → New → (fP.2-12 \nCreating New Entries b) \n■\tTo Add Scanned Number, etc. to an Existing \nPhone Book Entry\nHighlight a phone number, etc. → f (Select) \n→ Add to phonebook → Update → Search \nand select entry (fP.2-13) → Creating New Entries \n(fP.2-12) \n■\tTo Add Scanned URL to Bookmarks\nHighlight a URL → f (Select) → Add to \nbookmark → Enter a title\n■\tTo Copy Scanned Mail Address or Phone \nNumber, etc.\nHighlight mail address or phone number \n→ i → Copy → highlight the first character \n→ f (Start) → Highlight the last character → f \n(End) \n■\tTo Paste Scanned Phone Number, Mail \nAddress, etc. to Message Text\ni → Send → S! Mail or SMS → (fP.4-4 S! \nMail b, P.4-5 SMS b) \n■\tTo Copy Scanned Characters\ni → Copy → Highlight the first character → \nf (Start) → Highlight the last character → f \n(End) \nScanning Name Card & Setting to Save\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nName card reader → i (Settings) \n■ To Set Scan Method\nScan mode → Automatic scan/Manual Scan\n■ To Set Save Location\nSave to → Phonebook/Phone (vCard)/\nMemory Card (vCard) \n■\tTo Save Scanned Name Card Image to Phone \nBook\nAdd image → On/Off\nUsing Scanned Name Card\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nName card reader → Scan name card\n■\tTo Paste Scanned Text to Message\ni → Send → S! Mail/SMS → (fP.4-4 S! Mail \nb, P.4-5 SMS b) \n■\tTo Copy Scanned Character\ni → Copy → Highlight the first character → \nf (Start) → Highlight the last character → f \n(End) \n■\tTo Save Scanned Name Card to Notepad\ni → Save to Notepad → Edit memo → Select \ncategory → u (Save) \nAttaching Created QR Code to Message to Send\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nCreate QR code → Phonebook/My details/Text \ninput → (fP.9-11 Creating QR Code b) \n→ u (Send) → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \nUsing Saved Scanned Data\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nScan results → Select scanned result → i\n■\tTo Send Scanned Result\nSend → S! Mail or SMS → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b, \nP.4-5 SMS b) \n\n\n9-22\n9\nHandy Extras\n■\tTo Edit Text\nManual edit → Edit text → u (Save) \n■\tTo Copy Scanned Result\nCopy → Highlight the first character → f \n(Start) → Highlight the last character → f (End) \n■\tTo Save Scanned Result to Notepad\ni → Save to Notepad → Edit memo → Select \ncategory → i (Save) \nRenaming Scanned Data\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan \n→ Scan results → Highlight result → i → \nRename → Enter name\nViewing Scanned Data Detail\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nScan results → Highlight result → i → Detail\nDeleting Scanned Data\nf → Tools → Useful → Barcode/Scan → \nScan results\n■\tTo Delete a Selected Result\nHighlight result → i → Delete → Selected → \nYes\n■\tTo Delete Multiple Results\ni → Delete → Multiple → Check items → u \n(Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Results\ni → Delete → All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\nCurrency/Unit Conversion\nViewing Exchange Rate\nf → Tools → Useful → Converter → \nCurrency → u (Rate) \nChanging Exchange Rate\nf → Tools → Useful → Converter → \nCurrency → u (Rate) → Highlight a currency → \nf (Edit) → Enter rate → f (Save) \nAdding Currency Unit\nf → Tools → Useful → Converter → \nCurrency → u (Rate) → u (Add) → Enter \ncurrency unit name → Enter rate\nDeleting Added Currency Unit\nf → Tools → Useful → Converter → \nCurrency → u (Rate) → Highlight currency → \ni (Delete) \nSplit the Bill\nCalculating Price with Calculator\nIn Split the Bill window, highlight Total Cost → u \n(Calc) \nSaving Costs & Carry-over\nIn Split the Bill window, f (Save) → Yes\n・\n\t To save costs or carry-over, Total Cost and Number \nof People in A or B must be entered.\nVoice Recorder\nSetting Recorded Sound File as Ringtone, etc.\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → u (Set as) → Select a Ringtone\n・\n\t If Caller ringtone is selected, search and select \nentry (fP.2-13).\nMoving Recorded Sound File\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → i → Data folder\n■\tTo Move a File\nHighlight file → i → Move → Selected → \nSelect save location\n■\tTo Move Selected Files\ni → Move → Multiple → Check files → u \n(Move) → Select save location\n■\tTo Move All Files\ni → Move → All → Select save location\nCopying Recorded Sound File\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → i → Data folder \n■\tTo Copy a File\nHighlight file → i → Copy → Selected → \nSelect save location\n■\tTo Copy Selected Files\ni → Copy → Multiple → Check files → u \n(Copy) → Select save location\n■\tTo Copy All Files\ni → Copy → All → Select save location\n\n\n9-23\n9\nHandy Extras\nSending Recorded Sound File\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → i → Send\n■\tTo Send via Message\nVia message → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Send via Infrared\nVia infrared (fP.12-3) \nEditing Recorded Sound File Name\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → i → Rename → Enter file \nname\nViewing Recorded Sound File Details\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → i → Details\nDeleting Recorded Sound File\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → \nRecord a sound → i → Delete → Yes\nChanging Default Name at Saving\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → i \n→ Rec. settings → Default name → Enter file \nname\nChanging Recording Time\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → i \n→ Rec. settings → Recording time → Select an \nitem\n・\n\t If Other is selected, enter recording time.\nChanging Default Saving Location\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → i \n→ Rec. settings → Save to → Select an item\nViewing Previous Sound Files\nf → Tools → Useful → Voice recorder → i \n→ Data folder\n■\tTo Change View Mode\ni → View by → File name/Title\n■\tTo Sort Files\ni → Sort by → Select item\n■\tTo View Secret Voice Files\ni → Unlock temporarily → Enter Phone \nPassword → f (OK) \n■\tToggle Handset/Memory Card\ni → Memory switch → Phone+Memory card/\nPhone/Memory card\nFile Viewer\nDeleting Files\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer\n■\tTo Delete a File\nHighlight file → i → Delete → Selected → \nYes\n・\n\t Alternatively, in Details window, press i → \nDelete → Yes.\n■\tTo Delete Selected Files\ni → Delete → Multiple → Check files → u \n(Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Files\ni → Delete → All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\nToggling Standard View/Fullscreen View\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select \nfile → i → Full screen/Normal screen\n・\n\t Alternatively, press j.\nSearching Characters in Page\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Search → Enter keyword\n・\n After the search results appear, to find the next/\nprevious word in the document that matches the \nsame search word, press f (Next).\n・\n\t To exit the search mode, press c.\n・\n\t To try to search using other words without exiting, \npress i → Search.\n\n\n9-24\n9\nHandy Extras\nGoing to Pages\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Go to → Select an item\n・\n\t For Page, specify page number.\n・\n Use r to go to another page.\nRotating Display Image\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select \nfile → i → Rotate\n・\n\t Alternatively, press 3.\nCapturing Images\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Screen capture\n・\n\t Captured image is saved in JPEG format to Pictures \nin Data Folder of handset.\nSending Files\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Send\n■\tTo Send via Message\nVia message → (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Send via Infrared\nVia infrared (fP.12-3) \n・\n\t Alternatively, select File viewer → Highlight file \n→ i → Send → Via message/Via infrared.\nEditing File Name\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Rename → Enter file name\n・\n\t Alternatively, select File viewer → Highlight \nfile → i → Manage → Rename → Enter file \nname.\nProtecting File\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Lock or Unlock\n・\n Only files saved in handset are selectable.\n・\n Set file lock to restrict renaming, moving, or \ndeleting.\nViewing File Details\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Details \n・\n\t Alternatively, select File viewer → Highlight file \n→ i → Details.\nAssigning Scroll Range\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select \na file → i → Settings → Panning → Select an \nitem\nFitting to Display\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Settings → Reflow → On or Off\nSetting Map\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Settings → Map on → On or Off\n・\n\t Current position is framed in blue.\n・\n To view/hide map temporarily, in file viewer, press \nu (Show) / u (Hide).\nSetting Controller Display \nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select \nfile → i → Settings → Controller → On or \nOff\n・Set to On to show controller only for fullscreen.\nEditing Default File Name at Screen Capture\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select a \nfile → i → Settings → Screen capture name \n→ Enter file name\nViewing Shortcut Key\nf → Tools → Useful → File viewer → Select \nfile → Shortcut\n\n\n10\n\t \t Handset Security\nHandset Security.................................................................................. 10-2\nChanging Phone Password................................................................... 10-3\nChanging Phone Password..........................................................................10-3\nChanging PIN/PIN2.....................................................................................10-3\nPhone Lock........................................................................................... 10-3\nActivating/Canceling Phone Lock.................................................................10-3\nPassword Lock............................................................................................10-4\nActivating/Canceling PIN Code....................................................................10-4\nActivating/Canceling USIM Lock..................................................................10-4\nSecure Remote Lock....................................................................................10-5\nFunction Lock....................................................................................... 10-5\nActivating Function Lock.............................................................................10-5\nActivating/Canceling Secret Mode...............................................................10-5\nActivating/Canceling Secret Data Folder.\n......................................................10-5\nActivating Mobile Tracker.\n...........................................................................10-5\nRestoring Default Settings................................................................... 10-6\nClearing Phone Memory..............................................................................10-6\nResetting Settings.......................................................................................10-6\nAll Reset.....................................................................................................10-7\n\n\n10-2\nHandset Security\n10\nHandset Security\nThis handset features built-in security measures for safer handset use.\nLocking & Restricting Handset Operations\nFunction Lock\nRestoring Default Settings\nLock handset for information security. Handset operations cannot be executed \nwhile locked.\nActivate to require Phone Password to use Phone Book, Messaging, or other \nprivacy related functions.\nClear Phone Book entries; restore function settings to defaults.\nUse Phone Lock, Password Lock, or USIM Lock (fP.10-3).\n・\n\t Password\n* * * *\nSecrete data\n■■■■■■■\n■■■■■■■\n■■■■■■■\n■■■■■■■\n■■■■■■■\n■■■■■■■\nHide\n\n\n10-3\nHandset Security\n10\nChanging Phone Password\nThere are two security codes; Phone Password and \nPIN/PIN2.\nChanging Phone Password\nDefault: Phone Password is set to \"9999\".\na\tf → Settings → Security → \nChange password\nb\tEnter current Phone Password → \nf (OK) \nc\tEnter new Phone Password (four- \nto eight-digit) → f (OK) \nd\tEnter new Phone Password again \n→ f (OK) \nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Change Phone Password (rP.13-21) \nChanging PIN/PIN2\na\tf → Settings → Security → \nChange PIN or Change PIN2 \n・\n\tSet PIN certification to On to enable \nPIN code (fP.10-4).\nb\tEnter current PIN or PIN2 → \nf (OK) \nc\tEnter new PIN or PIN2 (four- to \neight-digit) → f (OK) \nd\tEnter new PIN or PIN2 again (four- \nto eight-digit) → f (OK) \nPhone Lock\nThe following lock functions are available: \n・\n Phone Lock\n・\n Password Lock\n・\n\tPIN Certification\n・\n USIM Lock\nActivating/Canceling Phone Lock\nActivate this function to require Phone Password \neach time handset is powered on.\na\tf → Settings → Security \nb\tPhone lock → On or Off\nc\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \n・\n\tAll operations including receiving calls are not \naccepted unless you enter Phone Password.\n\n\n10-4\nHandset Security\n10\nPassword Lock\nWhen active, press any key in Standby for Phone \nPassword entry window. Enter Phone Password to \ncancel Password Lock and access handset.\na\tf → Settings → Security\nb\tPassword lock → On\nc\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \n・\n\tEven if Password Lock is set, some operations such \nas receiving calls can be performed.\n・\n\tUpon Password Lock activation, Standby Display \nreappears. Press any key to show Phone Password \nentry window. Enter Phone Password to unlock, \nPassword lock is automatically set to Off.\nActivating/Canceling PIN Code\nPINs are security codes for USIM Card. For details, \nsee \"USIM Card\" (fP.1-4).\nTo activate PIN Certification each time the power is \nturned on, set this function to On.\nSetting\na\tf → Settings → Security\nb\tPIN certification → On or Off\nc\tEnter PIN → f (OK) \nCanceling\nIf PIN or PIN2 is incorrectly entered three consecutive \ntimes, PIN Lock or PIN2 Lock is activated to restrict \nhandset operations. \nNote\n・\n\t\nFor more information about PUK and PUK2, \ncontact SoftBank Mobile Customer Center, \nGeneral Information (fP.14-29).\n・Entering PUK incorrectly ten consecutive \ntimes activates PUK Lock. Purchase USIM \nCard reissue at a SoftBank Shop.\nTo cancel PIN Lock or PIN2 Lock, perform following \noperations.\na\tIn PUK Code entry window, enter \nPUK Code → f (OK) \nb\tEnter new PIN or PIN2 (four- to \neight-digit) → f (OK) \nc\tEnter new PIN or PIN2 again → \nf (OK) \nActivating/Canceling USIM Lock\nActivate this function to require USIM Password to \nuse handset with a different USIM Card.\na\tf → Settings → Security \nb\tUSIM lock → On or Off\nc\tEnter USIM Password (four- to \neight-digit) → f (OK) \n・\n\tTo set to On, enter USIM Password (four- \nto eight-digit) again and press f (OK).\n・\n\tUSIM Password is dedicated to USIM Card \nauthentication. If USIM Password matches, another \nUSIM Card can be used in handset. \nChange USIM Password each time USIM lock is \nset to On.\n・\n\tIf you forget USIM Password, insert USIM Card \nwith USIM lock set to On and reset all settings \n(fP.10-7).\n\n\n10-5\nHandset Security\n10\nSecure Remote Lock\nIf handset is lost, lock handset functions or clear \nhandset data remotely from PCs or other mobile \nphones. \nThe following functions are available in Secure \nRemote Lock. \n・\n\t Lock\n・\n\t Unlock\n・\n\t Clear data\n・\n\t Confirm handset status\n・\n\t Show history\n・\n\tFor details, see SoftBank Mobile Website, or \ncontact SoftBank Mobile Customer Center, General \nInformation (fP.14-29).\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Activate/Cancel Phone Lock (rP.13-21)\n●\n●Activate/Cancel Password Lock (rP.13-21)\n●\n●Activate/Cancel PIN Certification (rP.13-21)\n●\n●Change PIN (rP.13-21)\n●\n●Change PIN2 (rP.13-21)\n●\n●Activate/Cancel USIM Lock (rP.13-21)\nFunction Lock\nActivating Function Lock\nActivate this function to require Phone Password to \nopen Phone Book, Calendar/Notepad/Tasks, Yahoo! \nKeitai, Messages, Call Log, or Data Folder.\na\tf → Settings → Security → \nFunction lock\nb\tCheck functions → u (Save) \nc\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \nActivating/Canceling Secret Mode\nSelect Hide to activate this function and hide secret \nPhone Book entries, Messaging folders, Calendar \nschedules, or Tasks.\na\tf → Settings → Security → Secret \nmode\nb\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \nc\tShow or Hide\n・\n\tPowering off then back on activates Secret Mode.\nActivating/Canceling Secret Data Folder\nActivate Secret mode to see additional Secret \nfolders within Data Folder.\na\tf → Settings → Security → Secret \ndata folder\nb\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \nc\tShow or Hide\n・\n\tPowering off handset then back on activates \nSecret data folder.\nActivating Mobile Tracker\nActivate this function to send SMS notification to \na specified address when a different USIM Card is \ninserted. Specify up to two addresses.\na\tf → Settings → Security → \nMobile tracker\nb\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \nc\tSelect Activation field → On\nd\tSelect Recipients field\n\n\n10-6\nHandset Security\n10\ne\tSelect To field → Direct input → \nEnter address → u (Done) \n・\n\tTo enter an address from Phone Book, \nselect To field → Phonebook → Search \nand select entry (fP.2-13) \n→ Select a phone number.\nfSelect Sender field → Enter sender \nname\ng\tu (Save) \n・\n\tWhen a different USIM Card is inserted, \nSMS notification is sent to the specified \naddress upon handset activation. \nNothing appears on handset whose USIM \nCard is replaced. If Phone Password is \nincorrectly entered three consecutive times \nwhen trying to set Mobile Tracker, SMS \nnotification is also sent.\n・\n\tTo delete a recipient address, press f and \nselect Remove in e.\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Activate/Cancel Function Lock (rP.13-21) \n●\n●Activate/Cancel Secret Mode (rP.13-21) \n●\n●Set Secret Mode on Sub-folder in Data Folder \n(rP.13-21) \n●\n●Set Mobile Tracker (rP.13-21) \nRestoring Default Settings\nClearing Phone Memory\nClear Data Folder, Messaging, handset Phone Book \nentries, Calendar/Tasks, Notepad, or User Dictionary. \nAlternatively, clear all handset files at once.\na\tf → Settings → Memory settings \n→ Phone memory → u (Clear) \nb\tCheck items → u (Clear) \nc\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \n→ Yes\nResetting Settings\nReset settings to clear saved contents/settings and \nresort default settings.\nThe following settings are affected.\nItem\nAffected Settings\n－\n・\n\tAlarms\nSettings\n・\n\tEvery setting\nThe following settings are not affected.\nItem\nUnaffected Settings\n－\n・\n\tCalendar\nTools\n・\n\tTasks\n・\n\tExchange rate in Currency\n・\n\tNotepad\nData Folder\n・\n\tContents in each folder\nPhone\n・\n\tPhonebook\n・\n\tCall log\n・\n\tNumbers in My details\n・\n\tGroup name in Group \nsettings\n・\n\tFavorites\n・\n\tMail group \nSettings\nPhone settings ・\n\tUser dictionary\nSecurity\n・\n\tUSIM lock\n・\n\tPIN certification\n・\n\tChange PIN\n・\n\tChange PIN2\nCall settings\n・\n\tVoicemail on settings\n・\n\tCall forwarding on settings\n・\n\tCall waiting settings\n・\n\tCall barring settings\n・\n\tEdit Black list contents\nMessaging\n・\n\tMessages in folders\n\n\n10-7\nHandset Security\n10\na\tf → Settings → Security → Reset \n→ Reset settings\nb\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \n→ Yes\n・\n\tHandset restarts.\nAll Reset\nRestore handset to defaults and delete Phone Book \nentries (Phone), Call Log, Messaging, and Data \nFolder contents/settings. However, preinstalled files \nare not deleted.\na\tf → Settings → Security → Reset \n→ All reset\nb\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \n→ Yes\n・\n\tHandset restarts.\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Restore Settings to Default Values (rP.13-21) \n●\n●Delete Phone Book Entries, Messages, etc. \n(rP.13-21) \n\n\n11\n\t \t Data Folder & Memory Card\nData Folder.\n.......................................................................................... 11-2\nDefault Folders.\n...........................................................................................11-2\nViewing Files........................................................................................ 11-3\nUsing Image Viewer....................................................................................11-3\nZooming In/Out.\n..........................................................................................11-4\nSaving Face Link.........................................................................................11-4\nFace Link....................................................................................................11-5\nManaging Files/Folders........................................................................ 11-6\nCreating Folders.\n.........................................................................................11-6\nRenaming File/Folder.\n..................................................................................11-6\nMoving File/Folder......................................................................................11-6\nCopying Files/Folders.\n..................................................................................11-6\nDeleting Files/Folders..................................................................................11-7\nMemory Card.\n....................................................................................... 11-8\nInitializing Memory Card.............................................................................11-8\nMemory Card Installation............................................................................11-8\nViewing Memory Card Files.........................................................................11-9\nViewing Memory Status....................................................................... 11-9\nAdvanced Settings.\n............................................................................. 11-10\nViewing Files.\n............................................................................................11-10\nManaging Files/Folders.\n.............................................................................11-11\nMemory Status.\n.........................................................................................11-12\n\n\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11-2\n11\nData Folder\nHandset files are organized in folders according to file format.\nDefault Folders\nHandset automatically sorts files into these folders: \nOther documents\nDocument or graphic files \nrequiring File viewer \nfor use on handset, \nvcf files, vcs files, etc.\nMail Art\nImage related to message\nRing Songs・Tones\nVoice Recorder files, \ndownloaded music, \nand other sound files\nPictures\nMessage Templates\nMy Pictograms\nDownloaded Pictograms\nVideos\nDigital camera\nImage files captured \nwith handset Camera\nImage files captured\n with handset Camera \n(available only when \nMemory Card is inserted)\nMusic\nDownloaded Chaku-Uta®\nHandset video files\nS! Mail Templates\n\n\n11-3\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\n・\n Save up to 999 files/folders in each default folder.\n・\n\tIn a folder, use Memory status to confirm \nmemory. Alternatively, confirm memory in Settings \n(fP.11-9).\n・\n\tIn Data Folder, press i → Memory switch → \nPhone+Memory card/Phone/Memory card to \ntoggle Data Folder.\n・\n\t\n appears in some folders as downloaded site \nshortcut. Select the link to access website via \nYahoo! Keitai.\n・\n If files in one default folder are too large, handset \nperformance may fall.\nViewing Files\nView files in Data Folder, like image, animation, \netc. Select Data Folder, file list appears.\na\tf → Data Folder\nb\tSelect a file location\nc\tSelect a file in List window\n・\n\tFile List Indicators\n：Nontransferable\n：Nontransferable and unusable\n：Protected\n：Copy protected file \n (transferable, content key valid) \n：Copy protected file \n (transferable, content Key expired) \n：Copy protected file \n (nontransferable, content key valid) \n：Copy protected file \n (nontransferable, content key expired) \n：Used as Wallpaper/Ringtone, etc.\n・\n Nontransferable/copy protected files other than \npreinstalled ones cannot be used.\n・\n\tActivating Camera/Voice Recorder from \nData Folder\n-\t With Pictures folder open, activate Camera in \nCamera mode (fP.11-11).\n-\t With Videos folder open, activate Camera in \nVideo mode (fP.11-11).\n-\t With Ring Songs・Tones folder open, activate \nVoice Recorder (fP.11-11).\nUsing Image Viewer\nView images in Portrait or Landscape view. Wide \nimage is shown as small image to show entire image.\na\tf → Data Folder → Pictures\nb\tSelect a file\nc\tg to change image\n・\n\tSome images may not appear.\n\n\n11-4\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nZooming In/Out\na\tf → Data Folder → Pictures \n→ Select an image\nb\tf (Zoom) \nc\ti / u to zoom in/out\n・\n\tTo scroll window, use r.\nSaving Face Link\nLink images to Phone Book entries to place calls or\nmessage directly from still images. \nLink up to ten Phone Book entry items to a still \nimage.\nCapturing & Setting Still Images\na\tj\nb\ti → Settings → Settings → Setup \n→ Face link display → On → \nu (Done) \nc\tf (\n) \n・\n\tAvailable only when Face Link is On \nand Auto save is Off or On (Preview \nmanual).\n・\n\tIf captured image is recognized, frame \nappears.\n・\n\tIf Face Link has been saved, name appears. \nIf not, ? appears. \n・\n\tIf captured image is not recognized, frame \ndoes not appear. The image is saved and \nViewfinder reappears.\n・\n\tIf Auto save is On, image will be saved \nand Viewfinder will reappear.\nd\ti → Edit face link\ne\tSearch and select entry (fP.2-13) \nf\tf (OK) \nAdding Data to Saved Image\na\tf → Data Folder → Pictures\nb\tSelect a file\nc\ti → Face link\nd\ti → Add name tag\ne\tSearch and select entry (fP.2-13) \nf\ts to move name tag → f (Save) \n\n\n11-5\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nFace Link\nPlace a call or message via Face Link image.\nCalling/Messaging from Image Window\na\tf → Data Folder → Pictures \n→ Select file\nb\ti → Face link → f (\n) \n・\n\tIf multiple Face Links are set, use s to \nselect one.\nc\tPlace a call or message\n■\t To View Other Face Link Images\nThis person's photo\n■\t To Select Images to be Saved as Face \nLink Images\nThis person's photo → i → Add \n→ Select file → f (Register) \n・\n\tFor an image without Face Link, select \nThis person's photo → i → Add \n→ Select a file → Yes → Use s to \nmove name tag → f (Save).\n■\t To Search & Save Same Face Link \nImages\nThis person's photo → i → Face \nsearch → Yes\n■\t To Cancel Same Face Link Images\nThis person's photo → Highlight a file \n→ i → Remove → Selected → Yes\n・\n\tTo Cancel Multiple Face Link Images\nThis person's photo → i → Remove \n→ Multiple → Check files → u \n(Remove) → Yes\n・\n\tTo Cancel All Face Link Images\nThis person's photo → i → Remove \n→ All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\n■\t To Place a Voice Call\nCall\n■\t To Send Face Link Data via Message\nMail → (fP.4-4 S! Mail e) \n■\t To View Phone Book\nPhonebook\nSending Face Link Image via Message\na\tf → Data Folder → Pictures \n→ Select file\nb\ti → Face link → Highlight name \ntag\nc\ti → Send via message\nd\tSend (fP.4-4 S! Mail e) \nAdvanced\nbrP.11-10\n●\n●Viewing Slide Show\n●\n●Purchasing/Downloading Content Key\n●\n●Deleting File\n●\n●Confirming File Details\n●\n●Capturing Document View Page\n●\n●Going to PDF/DOC File View Pages\n●\n●Searching PDF/DOC File Text\n\n\n11-6\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nManaging Files/Folders\nMake sub-folder under default folders. Copy, \nmove, or delete folder or file.\nCreating Folders\nCreate sub-folder in default folders. \nUse Set secret to hide created folder.\na\tf → Data Folder\nb\tSelect default folder\nc\ti → Manage → Create folder\n・\n\tIf there is no sub-folder or file in the folder, \nmenu varies.\nd\tEnter folder name\n・\n\tWith Memory Card inserted, select Phone/\nMemory card → Enter folder name.\n・\n\tNew folder cannot be created in a created folder.\nRenaming File/Folder\na\tf → Data Folder\nb\tSelect default folder → Highlight a \nfile or sub-folder\nc\ti → Manage → Rename/Rename \nfolder\nd\tEnter name\n・\n Protected files cannot be renamed.\nMoving File/Folder\nWhen Memory Card is inserted, move files or sub-\nfolders between handset (Phone) and Memory Card.\nNote\n・\n\t\nProtected files cannot be moved. \n・\n\t\nDownloaded files may not appear/play \nproperly if moved to another device or if a \ndifferent USIM Card is inserted.\n・\n\t\nNontransferable and unusable files (\n), \nprotected files (\n), or nontransferable and \nCopy protected files (\n or \n) cannot be \nmoved to Memory Card.\na\tf → Data Folder\nb\tSelect default folder\nc\tHighlight a file or sub-folder → i \n→ Move\nd\tMove files or sub-folders\n■\t To Move an Item\nSelected\n■\t To Move Multiple Items\nMultiple → Check files or sub-folders \n→ u (Move) \n■\t To Move All Files/Sub-folders in the \nSame Folder\nAll\ne\tSelect a destination folder \n→ Move here\n・\n\tWhen Memory Card is inserted, select \nPhone or Memory card, then select a \nmove destination folder.\n・\n If file/sub-folder with the same name exists, text \nentry window appears; edit file/sub-folder name. \n・\n To move a file set for Wallpaper or Ringtone to \nMemory Card, a confirmation appears. Choose \nYes to release the setting and move the file. When \nmoving multiple or all files, choose No to move \nonly files without set functions. Press c / \ny (Cancel) to cancel moving. \nCopying Files/Folders\nPaste copied file in the folder/sub-folder, or paste \ncopied sub-folder in the folder. When Memory Card is \ninserted, copy folders between handset and Memory \nCard.\nNote\n・\n \nNontransferable files cannot be copied.\na\tf → Data Folder\nb\tSelect default folder\nc\tHighlight a file or sub-folder → i \n→ Copy\nd\tCopy file or sub-folder\n\n\n11-7\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\n■\t To Copy an Item\nSelected\n■\t To Copy Multiple Items\nMultiple → Check files or sub-folders \n→ u (Copy) \n■\t To Copy All Files/Sub-folders in the \nSame Folder\nAll\ne\tSelect a destination folder \n→ Paste here\n・\n\tWhen Memory Card is inserted, select \nPhone or Memory card, then select a \ncopy destination folder.\n・\n When pasting files/sub-folders in the same \nlocation as the original, numbers such as \"_001\" \nare automatically added to pasted file/sub-folder \nnames.\n・\n If file/sub-folder with the same name exists, text \nentry window appears; edit file/sub-folder name.\nDeleting Files/Folders\na\tf → Data Folder → Select a file \nlocation\nb\tHighlight a file in List window \n→ i → Delete\nc\tDelete a file\n■\t To Delete an Item\nSelected → Yes\n■\t To Delete Multiple Items\nMultiple → Check files → u (Delete) \n→ Yes\n■\t To Delete All Files in the Same Folder\nAll → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \n→ Yes\n・\n\tTo delete folder, highlight folder → i → Delete \nfolder → (Enter Phone Password → f (OK) as \nrequired) → Yes.\n・\n When deleting a file that is set to a function or \nprotected, a confirmation appears. Choose Yes \nto cancel the setting and delete the file. When \ndeleting multiple files, choose Yes → Except \nprotected to delete only files not set to functions \nand unprotected files.\n・\n\tWhen deleting files with Content Key, a \nconfirmation appears. Choose Yes to delete both \nfile and Content Key.\nAdvanced\nbrP.11-11\n●\n●Editing Image with Image Editor\n●\n●Sending Files\n●\n●Sorting Files\n●\n●Adding Sound Files/Video Files to Playlist\n●\n●Managing Content Key in Data Folder\n●\n●Deleting Content Key\n●\n●Setting Secret in Sub-folder\n●\n●Canceling Secret Setting Temporarily\n●\n●Activating Camera Mode\n●\n●Activating Video Mode\n●\n●Recording Sound\n●\n●Setting & Canceling File Lock\n●\n●Setting Images as Wallpaper, etc.\n●\n●Setting Sound File to Ringtone in Normal Mode\n●\n●Setting Video File to Ringtone in Normal Mode\n\n\n11-8\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nMemory Card\nHandset is compatible with microSD™ and \nmicroSDHC™ Memory Card. Purchase Memory Card \nto use Memory Card-related handset functions.\n・\n Use only recommended Memory Card. Other \nmemory cards may not perform properly. \n・\n Do not place labels or stickers on Memory Card. \nThese items may affect card performance or \nresult in lost information. \n・\n Never disassemble or modify Memory Card. \n・\n Do not expose Memory Card to strong impacts, \npressure or liquids. \n・\n Do not touch Memory Card terminals or expose \nthem to metal objects. \n・\n Do not expose Memory Card to dust, high \nhumidity, or excessive heat. \n・\n\tDo not use in the presence of corrosive gases. \n・\n\tAvoid heat sources and do not dispose of in fire. \n・\n Memory Card is a consumable item. Card \nperformance deteriorates with usage.\n・\n\tSoftBank Mobile recommends 64, 128, 256, 512 \nMB, 1, 2 GB microSD™/microSDHC™ Memory \nCards or 4, 8, 16 GB microSDHC™ Memory Cards.\nNote\nProtect Important Information\n・\n\tMemory Card files may be lost or damaged \nby accident or due to a malfunction. Back \nup entries and store separately. SoftBank \nMobile is not liable for damage from lost \nor altered information. \n・\n\tMemory Cards do not have Write Protection \nSwitch. There is a risk of accidental erasure or \noverwriting of files.\nInitializing Memory Card\nFormatting a Memory Card on handset deletes all \npreviously saved files, etc. Format Memory Card on \nhandset before use. \na\tf → Settings → Memory settings \n→ Memory card → u (Format) → \nEnter Phone Password → f (OK) \n→ Yes\nMemory Card Installation\nTurn handset power off before inserting or removing \nMemory Card.\nNote\n・\n\t\nDo not apply excessive force when \ninserting/removing Memory Card; may \ndamage Memory Card or handset. \n・\n\t\nTake care not to lose removed Memory Card. \n・\n\t\nAvoid touching/damaging Memory Card \ncontacts when inserting/removing it. \n・\n\t\nDo not remove battery/Memory Card while \ncard files are being accessed; may damage \nhandset/card or result in damaged/lost files. \nInserting\na\tOpen Port Cover\n\n\n11-9\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nb\tWith contacts up, insert Memory \nCard until it clicks\nContacts side up\nc\tClose Port Cover\nRemoving\na\tOpen Port Cover\nb\tPush Memory Card lightly until it \nclicks\nc\tCard pops out; remove it\nd\tClose Port Cover\nViewing Memory Card Files\na\tf → Data Folder\nb\ti → Memory switch → Memory \ncard\n・\n\tInset Memory Card before checking it.\n・\n\tTo check handset Data Folder, press i \n→ Memory switch → Phone.\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Check Memory Card Details (rP.13-22) \n●\n●Rename Memory Card (rP.13-22) \n●\n●Format Memory Card (rP.13-22) \n●\n●Set Default Memory to Phone/Memory Card \n(rP.13-22) \nViewing Memory Status\nView following information.\n・\n\tStatus of memory in Data Folder\n・\n\tStatus of message folder\n・\n\tStatus of Calendar or Tasks items registered\n・\n\tStatus of Notepad items\n・\n Status of Phone Book (handset and USIM Card) \na\tf → Settings → Memory settings \n→ Memory status\nb\tView each item\n■\t To View Data Folder Status\nData Folder → Phone memory/\nMemory card\n■\t To View Messaging Status\nMessaging\n・\n\tReceived, Drafts, Sent and Unsent \nMessage memory appears by Size.\n・\n\tPress i (Count) to see messaging \nmemory by Count.\n・\n\tUSIM Card SMS appears in Count only.\n\n\n11-10\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\n■\t To View Calendar/Tasks Status\nCalendar/Tasks\n■\t To View Notepad Status\nNotepad\n■\t To View Phone Book Entries\nPhonebook\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Confirm Total/Remaining Phone Memory (rP\n.13-22) \n●\n●Clear Phone Memory (rP.13-22)\n●\n●View Memory Status (rP.13-22) \nAdvanced Settings\nViewing Files\nViewing Slide Show\nf → Data Folder → Pictures → Highlight a \nfile in List window → f (View) → i → Slide \nshow\n・\n\t To pause/resume Slide Show, press f (Pause) / \nf (Restart).\n・\n\t To stop Slide Show, press u (Stop).\nPurchasing/Downloading Content Key\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Highlight a file → i → Manage \n→ Download Content key → Yes\nDeleting File\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → i → Delete → Yes\nConfirming File Details\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → i → Details\nCapturing Document View Page\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select file → i → Screen capture\n・\n\t Captured image is saved to Pictures folder.\nGoing to PDF/DOC File View Pages\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → i → Go to → Previous page/\nNext page/First page/Last page/Page\n・\n\t If Page is selected, specify page number.\nSearching PDF/DOC File Text\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → i → Search → Enter text\n・\n\t Words that match are highlighted. Press f (Next) \nto search next.\n\n\n11-11\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nManaging Files/Folders\nEditing Image with Image Editor\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → i → Edit → Image editor \n→ (fP.6-10 Editing Still Images d) \nSending Files\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Highlight a file → i → Send\n■\tTo Send via Message\nVia message (fP.4-4 S! Mail b) \n■\tTo Send via Infrared\nVia infrared → (fP.12-3) \nSorting Files\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location → i \n→ Sort by → Select an item\n・\n\t Sort by following order: \n-\t Descending order by date (Date) \n-\t File type (Type) \n-\t File name (Name) \n- Ascending order by file size (Size) \n-\t Title (Title) \n-\t Content Key status (Content key type) \n・\n\t Folders appear at the top of list.\n・\n\t When selecting Type, files are sorted in \nalphabetical order according to file extensions.\n・\n\t When selecting Name, files are sorted in order of \nnumerics → alphabets → Japanese syllabary.\n・\n\t Files in Message templates folders cannot be \nsorted by Type.\n・\n\t When selected Content key type, files appear as \nfollows: Unrestricted → Nontransferable → Copy \nProtected (content key valid) → Copy Protected \n(content key expired) → Invalid Nontransferable.\n・\n\t Files without title names cannot be sorted by Title.\nAdding Sound Files/Video Files to Playlist\nf → Data Folder → Ring Songs・Tones, \nMusic, or Videos → Highlight a file → i \n→ Manage → Add to playlist\n・\n To create a new playlist and add files to it, press \nu (New) in Add to Playlist window.\n・\n Adding to Playlist is unavailable for some files.\nManaging Content Key in Data Folder\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ i → Manage → Content key info → Select \nContent Key to view\n・\n\t When a folder containing a Content Key is opened, \nall Data Folder/Memory Card Content Keys appear.\n・\n If no files require Content Key, Content key info \ndoes not appear.\nDeleting Content Key\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location → i \n→ Manage → Content key info\n■\tTo Delete an Item\nHighlight a Content Key → i → Delete \n→ Selected → Yes\n■\tTo Delete all Items\ni → Delete → All → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Yes\n・\n If no files require Content Key, Content key info \ndoes not appear.\nSetting Secret in Sub-folder\nf → Data Folder → Select Sub-folder and save \nlocation → Highlight folder → i → Set secret \n→ Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \n・\n\t Only folder saved in handset is selectable.\n・\n\t To release the secret setting, press i → Unset \nsecret → Enter Phone Password → f (OK).\nCanceling Secret Setting Temporarily\nf → Data Folder → Select a folder location \n→ i → Unlock temporarily → Enter Phone \nPassword → f (OK) \nActivating Camera Mode\nf → Data Folder → Pictures → i → Take \nphoto\nActivating Video Mode\nf → Data Folder → Videos → i → Record \nvideo\nRecording Sound\nf → Data Folder → Ring Songs・Tones → \ni → Record sound\n\n\n11-12\nData Folder & Memory Card\n11\nSetting & Canceling File Lock\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Highlight a file → i → Lock/Unlock\n・\n Save file to handset to set file lock.\n・\n Set file lock to restrict renaming, moving, or \ndeleting.\nSetting Images as Wallpaper, etc.\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Select a file → i → Set as\n■\tTo Set Image as Wallpaper\nWallpaper → Preview image → f (Set) \n■\tTo Set Image as Incoming Image\nCaller ID → Search and select Phone Book \nentry (fP.2-13) → f (Set) \n・\n This setting is unavailable for some files.\nSetting Sound File to Ringtone in Normal Mode\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Highlight a file → i → Set as\n■\tTo Set to Ringtone for Each Function\nVoice ringtone/Message ringtone/Missed \ncall notification ringtone/S! Quick News \nringtone/Delivery report ringtone\n■\tTo Set as Ringtone for Phone Book Entry\nCaller ringtone → Search and select entry \n(fP.2-13) \n・\n If a Memory Card file is set as incoming image or \nRingtone, copy file to handset first confirmation \nappears. If file is copy protected, move file to \nhandset first confirmation appears. Choose Yes to \ncomplete setting. \n・\n\t Only copy protected MPEG4 AAC, AAC+, or \nEnhanced AAC+ files can be set. However, copy \nprotected files with play count restrictions cannot \nbe set.\nSetting Video File to Ringtone in Normal Mode\nf → Data Folder → Select a file location \n→ Highlight a file → i → Set as\n■\tTo Set to Ringtone for Voice Call\nVoice ringtone\n■\tTo Set to Ringtone for Phone Book Entry\nCaller ringtone → Select entry (fP.2-13) \n・\n If a Memory Card file is set, copy to handset \nconfirmation appears. For a copy protected file, \nmove to handset confirmation appears. Select Yes \nto complete settings.\n・\n\t Only copy protected MPEG4 AAC, AAC+, or \nEnhanced AAC+ files can be set. However, copy \nprotected files with play count restrictions cannot \nbe set.\nRegistering File to Other Functions\nf → Data Folder → Other documents \n→ Select vcf/vcs/vnt/opml file → f (Register) \n・\n Register vcf, vcs, vnt, opml, etc. files saved in Data \nFolder to Phone Book, Calendar, Notepad or RSS \nfeed.\nMemory Status\nDeleting Registered/Saved Data\nf → Data Folder → Memory status \n→ Phone/Memory card as required → Highlight \nitem → u (Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete an Item/Multiple Items\nCheck items → u (Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete all Items\ni (Mark all) → u (Delete) → Enter Phone \nPassword → f (OK) → Yes.\n・\n\t Alternatively, press f → Settings → Memory \nsettings → Memory status → Select item \n→ Phone memory/Memory card as required → \nu (Delete) → Yes → Select item → u (Delete) \n→ Yes.\n・\n Delete message folder messages, Data Folder files, \nCalendar/Tasks, Phone Book entries or Notepads.\n・\n If file (s) are locked or set for another function, a \nconfirmation appears.\n\n\n12\n\t \t Connectivity & File Backup\nFile Transfers & Backup.\n....................................................................... 12-2\nInfrared.\n................................................................................................ 12-3\nAligning Infrared Ports................................................................................12-3\nSending Files.\n..............................................................................................12-3\nReceiving Files............................................................................................12-4\nUSB Connection.\n................................................................................... 12-4\nUSB Connection..........................................................................................12-4\nSending/Receiving in Mass Storage.\n.............................................................12-5\nMemory Card Backup........................................................................... 12-5\nBackup Precautions.\n....................................................................................12-5\nBacking up to Memory Card Manually.........................................................12-6\nLoading from Memory Card.\n........................................................................12-6\nBacking up to Memory Card Automatically..................................................12-6\nS! Addressbook Back-up (SAB).\n............................................................ 12-7\nBefore Using S! Addressbook Back-up.\n........................................................12-7\nPrecautions for Synchronizing......................................................................12-7\nSynchronizing Phone Book Entries...............................................................12-8\nSetting Auto Sync.\n.......................................................................................12-8\nAdvanced Settings.\n............................................................................... 12-9\nS! Addressbook Back-up.............................................................................12-9\n\n\n12-2\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nFile Transfers & Backup\nTransfer files via Infrared, etc. Use S! Addressbook Back-up (SAB)* to back up handset Phone Book entries.\n*S! Addressbook Back-up requires separate subscription.\nFile Transfers\nFile Backups\nUse these functions to transfer handset files: \n・\n\t Infrared (fP.12-3).\n・\n\t USB Connection (fP.12-4).\nBack up handset files to Memory Card or PC (fP.12-5).\nBack up Phone Book entries to Server via S! Addressbook Back-up.\nRestore lost Phone Book entries from S! Addressbook Back-up.\nEdit SAB via PC (fP.12-7).\nAccount Details\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\n9\n*\n0\n#\n\n\n12-3\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nInfrared\nExchange files wirelessly with infrared-compatible \nhandsets, PCs or other devices.\n・\n Handset Infrared is based on IrMC1.1. \nTransmissions may be unavailable for some \nfunctions, even when IrMC1.1 is supported on \nthe other party's handset.\n・\n\tTransmissions may be inhibited in direct \nsunlight, under fluorescent lighting or near \ninfrared devices.\n・\n\tSend and receive Phone Book entries or Calendar \nentries, Account Details, Schedules, Tasks, still \nimages, videos, sound files, music files, etc. \nSend either all Phone Book entries, Calendar/Tasks \nor Bookmarks/Notepad/Received msg./Drafts/Sent \nmsg. in a single transfer. \n・\n\tAuthorization Code is a four-digit code used to \nexecute infrared file transfers between devices. \nEnter same Authorization Code on both devices \nwhen using Transfer All. \nNote\n・\n\t\nInfrared is unavailable while Internet \nservices are in use, or while editing \nmessages/files. \n・\n\t\nSome received files cannot be saved on \nhandset.\nAligning Infrared Ports\n・\n\t Place devices within 30 cm. Align device ports. Do \nnot place objects in between devices. \nWithin 30cm\nInfrared Port\n・\n\t Maintain port alignment until transmission ends.\n・\n\t A soiled port may inhibit transmission. Clean port \nwith a soft cloth beforehand. \n・\n\t If transfer fails, a confirmation appears: \"Device \nnot found Reconnect?\" Choose Yes to retry.\nSending Files\nFirst, activate Infrared on the other device. \nSending Items One at a Time\na\tf → Infrared → Transfer files\nb\tSelect folder → Check files\nc\tu (Send)\n・\n\tAlternatively, in list, i → Send → Via infrared \n→ Check files → u (Send).\n・\n\tIn Details/Playback window, i → Send → Via \ninfrared.\n \nTransferring All\na\tf → Infrared → Transfer all\nb\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK)\nc\tPhonebook, Calendar/Tasks, \nBookmarks, Notepad, Received \nmsg., Drafts or Sent msg.\n・\n\tFor Phonebook, choose Yes to transfer \nimages. \nd\tEnter Authorization Code (four-\ndigit) → f (OK)\n\n\n12-4\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nReceiving Files\nNote\n・\n\t\nFiles cannot be received when Key Lock is \nactive or during Software Update. \nReceiving One Item at a Time\na\tf → Infrared → Receive\n・\n\tHandset is ready to receive files.\nb\tBegin sending from other device \nwithin three minutes \nc\tSave confirmation appears, choose Yes\n・\n\tTo save image file, choose Pictures or \nMail Art.\n・\n\tTo save pictograms, choose Pictures, Mail \nArt or My Pictograms.\n・\n\tPress i (Cancel) to cancel receiving.\n・\n\tPress y to terminate reception.\n・\n\tIf vcf file contains incoming image exceeding 100KB, \nhandset deletes the image then saves it in Phone \nBook.\nReceiving All \na\tf → Infrared → Receive\n・\n\tHandset is ready to receive files. \nb\tBegin sending from other device \nwithin three minutes\nc\tEnter Authorization Code (four-\ndigit) → f (OK)\n・\n\tEnter same Authorization Code as sender. \nd\tSelect a saving method\n■\t To Add Files as New Entries\nAdd new\n■\t To Overwrite Current Entries\nDelete & Overwrite → Yes → Enter \nPhone Password → f (OK)\n・\n\tReceiving all entries deletes existing \nhandset entries except for Account Details. \nReceiving Account Details deletes existing \nAccount Details except for handset phone \nnumber.\n・\n\tPress i (Cancel) to cancel receiving. \n・\n\tPress y to terminate reception. \nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Receive Infrared Transmission (rP.13-23)\n●\n●Transfer Account Details (rP.13-23)\n●\n●Transfer Files (rP.13-23)\n●\n●Transfer All Phone Book Entries, Calendar/Tasks , \nBookmarks, Notes or Messages at Once (rP.13-23) \nUSB Connection\nConnect handset to PC to transfer files between \ndevices. \nHandset supports USB 2.0.\nInstall USB driver first. For installation instructions, \nPC operating environment, etc., access SAMSUNG \nWebsite (http: //jp.samsungmobile.com/pc/\nlineup/001download.html).\nUSB Connection\nThe following operations are available: \n・\n\t Transfer handset Data Folder files to PC\n・\n\t Import PC files and save to Data Folder\n・\n\t Perform Packet Communications\nNote\n・\n\t\nUsing handset to access the Internet via \nPC or PDA (Mobile Data Communication) \nrapidly incurs high Packet Communication \ncharges. Take notice of large Packet \nCommunications when using Mobile Data \nCommunication.\n\n\n12-5\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nSending/Receiving in Mass Storage\nWith Memory Card inserted, connect handset to PC \nvia USB Cable to manage card files on PC.\nConnecting/Disconnecting to a PC\na\tConnect handset to PC via USB \nCable\nb\tf → Settings → Connectivity \n→ Mass storage → Yes\nc\tEnter Phone Password → f (OK)\nd\tUse PC to access Memory Card files\n・\n\tMass Storage is unavailable while receiving \nS! Mail, or using Samsung New PC Studio.\n・\n\tCalling and Messaging are unavailable in \nMass Storage.\ne\tOn PC, perform device removal\nf\tIn Mass storage, i (Exit)\ng\tDisconnect USB Cable\nNote\n・\n\t\nNever disconnect USB Cable before safely \nremoving device from the PC first.\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Activate Mass Storage (rP.13-23)\nMemory Card Backup\nBack up Phone Book entries, etc. to Memory Card \n(package backup). Restore backed up items as \nrequired (package restoration).\n・\n\tRestore from Backup in case of accidental data loss.\n・\n\tBackups are saved by type (transfer date is file name).\n・\n\tAvailable Backup types\n-\t Phone Book\n-\t Sent msg.\n-\t Calendar\n-\t Unsent msg.\n-\t Tasks\n-\t Notepad\n-\t Received msg.\n-\t Contents keys\n-\t Drafts\n-\t Bookmarks\n・\n Use Backup to save files, share information \nbetween Memory Card-compatible handsets, or \nmove files to a newly purchased handset.\nBackup Precautions\n・\n\t Unavailable when battery is low.\n・\n\t During backup or restoration, handset \ntransmissions are not possible.\n・\n\t Some files cannot be backed up. Some backed \nup files may not be usable on other SoftBank \nhandsets or PCs, etc.\n・\n\t Backup may fail if handset/Memory Card memory \nis too low.\n・\n\t Handset holds up to 500 Calendar/Tasks entries. \nWhen 500 entries are restored from Memory \nCard, a confirmation appears and extra entries \nare not saved.\n・\n\t Yahoo! Keitai, PC Site Browser bookmarks are \nbacked up.\n・\n\t If a backed up bookmark is too large it may not \nbe restorable.\n・\n\t Some images set to Phone Book entries may not \nbe transferred because of size.\n・\n\t Backup data saved on Memory Card is not \naccessible on handset until restored from Memory \nCard.\n・\n\t When backing up Content Keys, note the \nfollowing: \n-\t Backup file can hold only one Content Key \nat a time. To back up another Content Key, a \nconfirmation appears and the previous backup \nfile is overwritten (to keep the previously \nbacked up files, restore the Content Key to \nhandset from Memory Card and then perform \nbackup again).\n-\t Restoring a file with a Content Key to handset \nadds the Content Key to handset without \noverwriting any existing Content Keys on \nhandset.\n\n\n12-6\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nBacking up to Memory Card Manually\na\tf → Settings → Backup & Restore \n→ Backup\nb\tYes → Enter Phone Password → f \n(OK)\nc\tPhonebook, Calendar, Tasks, \nReceived msg., Drafts, Sent msg., \nUnsent msg., Notepad, Contents \nkeys or Bookmarks\nd\tConfirmation appears, choose Yes\n・\n\tPress i (Cancel) → Yes to cancel backup.\n・\n\tIf Contents keys backup file already \nexists, an overwrite confirmation appears. \nPress u (Yes) to overwrite the file.\nLoading from Memory Card\nSelecting Item to Back up\na\tf → Settings → Backup & Restore \n→ Restore\nb\tYes → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Selected item\nc\tPhonebook, Calendar, Tasks, \nReceived msg., Drafts, Sent msg., \nUnsent msg., Notepad, Contents \nkeys or Bookmarks\nd\tSelect a file → If a confirmation \nappears, Add/Overwrite\n・\n\tTo delete a backup file, highlight file \n→ i (Delete) → Yes.\n・\n\tTo cancel restoration, press i (Cancel) \n→ Yes.\nBacking up from Auto Back up\na\tf → Settings → Backup & Restore \n→ Restore\nb\tYes → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Auto backup item\nc\tSelect item → Yes\n・\n\tTo cancel backup, press i (Cancel) \n→ Yes.\nBacking up to Memory Card Automatically\nNote\n・\n\t\nSeparate subscription is required to use \nthis function.\n・\n\t\nBefore setting, set Auto sync settings to On \nin S! Addressbook Back-up setting (fP.12-8).\n・\n\t\nDefault: Auto backup is On, and Backup \ncycle is Every week.\n・\n\t\nAuto Backup starts only when Handset is in \nStandby.\n・\n\t\nIf Auto Backup is disturbed, it starts at the \ntime set for the next day.\na\tf → Settings → Backup & Restore \n→ Auto backup\nb\tBackup cycle\nc\tCycle\n■\t To Back up Once a Week\nWeekly → Select day\n■\t To Back up Once a Month\nMonthly → Enter date\nd\tStart time → Enter start time \n→ c\ne\tBackup items → Check items \n→ u (Save)\nf\tEncryption settings → Phonebook/\nCalendar/Tasks/Messages/Notepad/\nBookmarks → On/Off\nAdvanced\ns\n●\n●Back up Memory (rP.13-22)\n●\n●Restore Memory (rP.13-22)\n\n\n12-7\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nS! Addressbook Back-up (SAB)\nBack up handset Phone Book entries on Server or \nsynchronize handset Phone Book entries with SAB. \nRestore lost handset Phone Book entries from SAB.\nBackup/Restore\nSynchronize\nPhone Book\nServer\nImport/Export\nEdit Phone Book\non PC\nBefore Using S! Addressbook Back-up\nNote\n・\n\t\nSAB use requires separate subscription.\n・\n\t\nConnections between handset and SAB \n(Backup, Restore, or Update) incur Packet \nCommunication charges.\n・\n If you should change handsets, select an SAB \ncompatible handset to take over SAB entries.\n・\n After an application, when Network Information \nis retrieved*, Auto sync settings will be On \nautomatically. After editing Phone Book, backup \nwill start automatically.\n・\n\tEven after Auto sync settings is set to Off, if \nNetwork Information is retrieved Auto Sync will \nbe initialized and set to On.\n・\n\tConfirm Auto sync settings is set to Off after \ncanceling the services.\n*Sync mode will be set to Normal. Auto Sync \nstarts about ten minutes after editing of Phone \nBook has begun.\nPrecautions for Synchronizing\nAvailable synchronization modes are as follows.\nSync Mode\nDescription\nNormal\nBacks up handset entries and \nupdates SAB. If handset Phone \nBook entry and SAB entry item \nare both updated, SAB entry item \ntakes priority.\nSync from Client\nBacks up updated handset \nentries.\nBackup\nDeletes SAB entries and uploads \nhandset entries.\nSync from Server\nDownloads updated SAB entries \nto handset.\nRestore\nDeletes all the latest handset \nentries and downloads SAB \nentries to handset (only the \n001SC).\n・\n\tSynchronizing in Normal mode is performed \nregardless of Sync mode setting when using \nSAB for the first time or the last Sync was not \ncompleted correctly by canceling, etc.\n・\n\t These items cannot be synchronized with SAB; \nusing Restore for these items will delete them \nfrom handset: \n-\t Picture\n-\t Ringtone settings, Vibration settings\n-\t Blood type\n\n\n12-8\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nSynchronizing Phone Book Entries\nConnect to SAB to synchronize SAB entries with \nhandset Phone Book entries.\nNote\n・\n\t\nStarting Sync connect to network. Packet \nCommunication charges apply. Network \nconnection is automatically disconnected \nwith synchronization. \na\tf → Phone → S! Addressbook \nBack-up → Start sync\n・\n\tSynchronize in Normal mode.\n・\n\tIf synchronize in Sync from Client/\nBackup/Sync from Server/Restore \nmode, press f → Phone → S! \nAddressbook Back-up → Details \n→ Backup/Restore → Select an item.\n・\n\tAlternatively, press f → Entertainment \n→ S! Addressbook Back-up → Start \nsync.\n・\n\t Select backup/restore timing and Sync mode \ncarefully to avoid accidentally deleting entries.\n-\t Delete all handset entries then select Normal, \nSync from Client, or Backup to delete all \nSAB entries.\n-\t Delete all SAB entries then select Normal, \nSync from Server, or Restore to delete all \nhandset entries.\n・\n\t If number of entry items savable on handset \nvaries from SAB, synchronization will reflect lower \nnumber.\n・\n\t When SAB service is canceled, Phone Book \nentries on Server are deleted.\nSetting Auto Sync\nIf Auto sync settings is set to On, setting \nfrequency and Sync mode are required.\na\tf → Phone → S! Addressbook \nBack-up → Details → Auto sync \nsettings\n・\n\tAlternatively, press f → Entertainment \n→ S! Addressbook Back-up → Details \n→ Auto sync settings.\nb\tOn/Off → On\nc\tSet items\n■\t To Back up Once a Month\nMonthly → In Date field, enter date \n→ In Time field, enter time → f (OK)\n■\t To Back up Once a Week\nWeekly → Select day → In Time field, enter \ntime → f (OK)\n■\t To Back up Ten Minutes after Editing \nPhone Book Entries\nAfter editing phonebook\nd\tNormal/Sync from Client/Backup/\nSync from Server/Restore\ne\tf (OK)\n・\n\tIn b, set On/Off to Off to cancel Auto sync \nsettings.\n\n\n12-9\nConnectivity & File Backup\n12\nAdvanced Settings\nS! Addressbook Back-up\nViewing S! Addressbook Back-up History\nf → Phone → S! Addressbook Back-up \n→ Details → Sync Log → Select a log\nDeleting S! Addressbook Back-up History\nf → Phone → S! Addressbook Back-up \n→ Details → Sync Log\n■\tTo Delete A Log\nHighlight log → u (Delete) → Yes\n■\tTo Delete All Logs\ni (Delete all) → Enter Phone Password\n→ f (OK) → Yes\n\n\n13\n\t \t Handset Customization\nPhone Settings..................................................................................... 13-2\nHandset Settings.........................................................................................13-2\nSounds & Vibration & External Light Settings..................................... 13-4\nDisplay & Font Settings.\n....................................................................... 13-5\nManner Mode Settings.\n........................................................................ 13-7\nCall Settings......................................................................................... 13-7\nPhone Book Settings.......................................................................... 13-10\nMessaging Settings............................................................................ 13-11\nCustom Mail Address................................................................................13-11\nS! Mail & SMS.\n..........................................................................................13-11\nS! Mail.\n.....................................................................................................13-13\nSMS.\n.........................................................................................................13-14\nInternet Settings................................................................................ 13-15\nYahoo! Keitai.\n...........................................................................................13-15\nPC Site Browser........................................................................................13-16\nCamera Settings................................................................................. 13-18\nPhoto.\n.......................................................................................................13-18\nVideo.\n.......................................................................................................13-19\nMedia Player Settings........................................................................ 13-19\nMusic.\n.......................................................................................................13-19\nMovie.......................................................................................................13-20\nEntertainment Settings...................................................................... 13-20\nS! Information Channel.............................................................................13-20\nSecurity Settings................................................................................ 13-21\nMemory Settings................................................................................ 13-22\nConnectivity Settings......................................................................... 13-23\nInfrared.\n....................................................................................................13-23\nUSB..........................................................................................................13-23\nNetwork...................................................................................................13-23\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-2\n13\nPhone Settings\nHandset Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Phone settings\nChange User Interface Language\b\no Automatic 言語選択 → Select an item\nSet Time Zone Updating\b\no Manual only\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Time zone updating → Select an item → u (Save) \nChange Home Zone Time\b\no GMT+09: 00\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Home zone → g to highlight city → f (Select) \n→ u (Save)\n・\n Select the zone closest to your locality.\nActivate/Cancel Daylight Savings Time\b\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Home zone → g to highlight city → Highlight \nDaylight saving → u (Mark) → f (Select) → u (Save) \nSet Time\nDate & Time → Set date & time → In Time field, enter time → u (Save)\n・\n Some functions are disabled when time is not set.\nSet Date\nDate & Time → Set date & time → In Date field, enter date → u (Save)\n・\n Some functions are disabled until date is set.\nChange Time Format\b\no 24 H\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Time format → Select an item → u (Save) \nChange Date Format\b\no YYYY/MM/DD\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Date format → Select an item → u (Save) \nSet Time Correction\no Auto correction: On, Correction timing: Via S! Information Channel\nDate & Time → Time correction → Auto correction → On or Off\n・\n To specify when to correct the time, select Correction timing → Check an item → u (Save).\n・\n Selecting Manual correction → Yes immediately corrects the time.\nSet Earphone Settings\b\no Earphone\nEarphone settings → Earphone/Earphone + Speaker\nActivate/Cancel Prediction\b\no On Text input settings → Prediction → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Learning\b\no On Text input settings → Learning → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Auto Capitalization\b\no On Text input settings → Auto capitalization → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Flexible Search\b\no On Text input settings → Flexible search → On or Off\nReset Learning Function\nText input settings → Reset learning → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-3\n13\nClear History for Pictograms/Emoticons\nText input settings → Clear history → Yes\nChange Font Size\b\no Standard Text input settings → Font size → Large/Standard/Small\nChange Cursor Speed\b\no Off\nText input settings → Auto cursor → Off/Slow/Normal/Fast/Very fast\nSave Entries to User Dictionary\nUser dictionary → Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → New entry (If more than \none entry is saved, press u (Add) ) → Select Word field → Enter word or sentence → Select \nReading field → Enter reading → u (Save) \nEdit User Dictionary Entries\nUser dictionary → Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → Select entry → Edit word \nand reading → u (Save) \nDelete User Dictionary Entries\nUser dictionary → Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → Highlight word → i \n→ Delete → Selected → Yes\n・\n To delete several words, select Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → i → Delete \n→ Multiple → Check words → u (Delete) → Yes.\n・\n To delete all the words, select Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → i → Delete \n→ All → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes.\nActivate/Cancel Simple Search \b\no Off\nSimple search → On or Off\n・\n On: In Standby, press keys assigned to characters used in Phone Book entry Readings.\nSet Any Key Answer\b\no Off\nAny key answer → On or Off\n・\n On: Press any keys except u, f, s, i, y and c to answer a call. \nAnswer Incoming Call by Opening Handset\b\no Off\nActive folder → On or Off\n・\n On: Open the handset to answer a call. \nSet Keypad Light Illumination Mode\b\no Normal mode\nKeypad light → Select item\n・\n Normal mode: Keypad light illuminates for Backlight time duration.\n・\n Saving mode: Keypad light turns off for set duration.\n・\n If Saving mode is set, in Starting time field, enter start time → In Ending time field, enter \nend time → u (Save).\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-4\n13\nSounds & Vibration & External Light Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Sound settings\nAdjust Volume\no Voice call/Message/Missed call notification/Delivery report/Phone \nsounds: Level 3; S! Quick News: Off\nVolume → Select item → s to adjust image\n・\n If Ringtone reducer is On (fP.13-10), Ringtone volume is reduced to Level 1 for the first four \nseconds, regardless of Ringtone volume set for Voice Call.\n・\n To mute Voice Call or Message tones, set Volume to 00 and Vibration to Off. \n appears.\nSet Ringtone for Voice Call\n\b\no Voice call: Samsung Tune\nRingtone → Voice call → Select save location for a file → Select a file\n・\n Press u (Play) to playback.\nSet Ringtone to Something Other than Voice Call\no Message: Good_morning; Missed call notification: Bubble; S! \nQuick News: Postman; Delivery report: Doorbell\nRingtone → Select item → Ringtone → Select save location for a file → Select a file\n・\n Press u (Play) to playback.\nSet Ringtone Duration to Something Other than Voice Call\n\b\no 5 Seconds\nRingtone → Select item → Duration → Enter duration → f (Select) \nSearch Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → Music search → Follow onscreen instructions\nSet Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → Settings → Follow onscreen instructions\nRegister/Cancel Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → Register/Cancel → Follow onscreen instructions\nView Instruction for Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → What's Machi-Uta\nSet Vibration\b\no Off Vibration → Select item → Select a pattern\n・\n Press u (Play) to view a pattern.\nSet Phone Sounds\b\no Off\nPhone sounds → Keypad tones → Select item\nSet System Sounds\no Popup box alerts/Call end tone/Alerts on call: On; Minute minder/\nCall connect tone/Power on/Power off/Open/Close folder: Off\nPhone sounds → System sounds → Check items → u (Save)\n・\n Available items vary depending on mode.\nSet External Light Color for Incoming Transmissions\no Voice call/Missed call notification: Blue; Message: Green; S! Quick \nNews: White; Alarm: Pink; Delivery report: Light Blue\nExternal light → Incoming → Select an item → Select a color\n・\n When selecting Off, Notification light does not blink.\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-5\n13\nSet External Light Color for Notification\no Missed call/Missed call notification: Blue; Message: Green; \nAnswering Machine: Yellow; Missed alarm: Pink; Delivery report: Light blue\nExternal light → Notification → Select an item → Select a color \n・\n When selecting Off, Notification light does not blink.\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\nSet External Light Color When Handset is Closed\b\no Pink\nExternal light → Close folder → Select a color\n・\n When selecting Off, Notification light does not blink.\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\n・\n\tOpen Sound settings to change sounds for Normal mode. Settings cannot be changed for other modes.\nDisplay & Font Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Display settings\nChange Wallpaper\b\no Clover Wallpaper → (fP.2-5 Wallpaper b) \nSet/Cancel Smart Wallpaper\b\no On\nSmart wallpaper → On/Off → On or Off\nChange Wallpaper for Smart Wallpaper\nSmart wallpaper → Wallpapers → Select item → Select Wallpaper\nChange Main Menu Settings\b\no Standard\nMain menu style → Select an item → (g to select color, as required) → f (Select) \nSet Menu Color Theme\b\no White & Blue\nColor theme → Select an item\nChange Clock/Calendar\b\no Digital clock\nClock/Calendar → Select an item\n・\n If Digital clock is selected, in Style field, highlight style → In Position field, highlight position \n→ f (Save).\n・\n If Dual clock is selected, in First clock field, highlight time zone → In Second clock field, \nhighlight time zone → f (Save).\n・\n If Calendar (1 month) is selected, select Large/Small. \nSet Mini Clock\b\no Time only\nMini clock → Select an item\nSet Font Weight\b\no Regular\nFont → Font weight → Select an item\nSet Text Size in List Font\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → List font → Select item\nSet Text Size in Yahoo! Keitai Pages\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Yahoo! Keitai → Select an item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-6\n13\nSet Text Size in PC Site Browser\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → PC site browser → Select an item\nSet Text Size in Phone Book\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Phonebook → Select item\nSet Text Size in Editor\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Editor → Select item\nChange Message Text Font Size\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Messages → Select an item\nChange Text Scroll Speed for Menu List\b\no Normal Text scroll speed → Fast/Normal/Slow\nAdjust Display Brightness\b\no Auto adjustment\nBacklight → Brightness → i (Unmark) → g to adjust brightness → f (OK) \nSet Backlight Time\b\no 15 seconds\nBacklight → Duration → Backlight on → Select an item\n・\n When Backlight time is set to Off, Display becomes dim.\n・\n Display becomes dimmer when Backlight time elapses.\nSet Backlight Dimmer Time\b\no 15 seconds\nBacklight → Duration → Backlight dim → Select an item\n・\n When Backlight time elapses, Display turns off.\nSet Battery Saving Mode\b\no On\nBattery saving mode → On or Off\nSet Text Type in Dialling Display\b\no Normal\nDialling display → Font type → g to highlight type → f (Select) \nSet Text Size in Dialling Display\b\no Standard\nDialling display → Font size → g to highlight size → f (Select) \nSet Text Color in Dialling Display\b\no Basic\nDialling display → Font color → g to highlight color → f (Select)\n・\n If Monochrome is highlighted in Color field, select color.\nSet Background Color in Dialling Display\nDialling display → Background color → g to highlight color → f (Select) \nSet Operator Name\b\no Off\nOperator name → On or Off\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-7\n13\nManner Mode Settings\nSwitch Manner Mode\nf → Settings → Manner mode settings → Select mode\n・\n To edit each setting in Manner mode, highlight mode → u (Edit) → Set each item.\nCall Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Call settings\nForward All Calls to Voicemail (Handset Does Not Ring) \nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Voicemail on → Always (0 sec.) \nForward Unanswered Calls to Voicemail (Specify Ring Time) \nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Voicemail on → No reply (5 - 30 \nsec.) \nActivate & Set Forwarding\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Call forwarding on → Select an \nitem → Set number to forward (fP.3-14 Call Forwarding c) \nCancel Voicemail/Call Forwarding\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Deactivate All → Yes\nConfirm Current Voicemail/Call Forwarding Settings\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Get status\nListen to Voicemail Message\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Play voicemail → t or f \n(\n) \nActivate/Cancel Call Waiting\nOptional services → Call waiting → On or Off\nConfirm Current Call Waiting Settings\nOptional services → Call waiting → Get status\nActivate/Cancel Outgoing Call Barring\nOptional services → Call barring → Outgoing call → Select an item → On or Off \n→ Enter Network Password → f (OK) \nActivate/Cancel Incoming Call Barring\nOptional services → Call barring → Incoming call → Select an item → On or Off \n→ Enter Network Password → f (OK) \nCancel All Call Barring\nOptional services → Call barring → Cancel all barring → Enter Network Password → \nf (OK) → Yes\nConfirm Current Call Barring Settings\nOptional services → Call barring → Get status → Select an item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-8\n13\nSet Missed Call Notification\nOptional services → Missed call notification → t or u (\n) → Follow the \nguidance \nCheck Call Time/Cost\nCall time & cost → All calls\n・\n To reset call time/cost, press u (Reset) → Enter PIN2 → f (OK).\nCheck Last Call Time/Cost\nCall time & cost → Last call\n・\n To reset last call time/cost, press u (Reset).\nCheck Data Counter\nCall time & cost → Data counter\n・\n To reset sent/received data counter, press u (Reset).\nShow/Hide Call Time/Cost after Calls\b\no Off\nCall time & cost → Show charge after call → On or Off\n・\n This function may not be available.\nChange Call Cost Currency\nCall time & cost → Set currency → Enter PIN2 → f (OK) → In Price field, enter rate in yen \n→ Select currency field → Enter currency unit → u (Save) \nActivate/Cancel Answering Machine\b\no Off\nAnswering machine → On/Off → On or Off\nSet Answering Machine Response Time\b\no 18seconds\nAnswering machine → Ringing duration → Select an item\n・\n If Other is selected, enter time.\nPlay Answering Machine Records\nAnswering machine → Play message → Select a record\n・\n To delete record, in list, highlight record → u (Delete) → Yes.\n・\n Alternatively, press t → All/Received → Select a record → u (\n) → Message.\nSet Answering Machine Response Language\b\no 日本語\nAnswering machine → Sound language → Select an item\n・\n Press u (Play) to play message.\nAccept/Reject Calls from Specified Phone Numbers\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Set reject number → On/Off → On or Off\n・\n When a call on Black list is received, the caller hears a busy tone and call is not connected. \nMissed call appears in Standby. Select the message to check missed call.\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-9\n13\nCreate/Edit Black List\nReject incoming calls → Set reject number → Black list → f (Add) (If more than one \nentry is added, press i → Add) → Select an item → Add an entry\n・\n \t\nTo delete a phone number, select Black list → Highlight party → i → Delete → \nSelected → Yes.\n・\n \t\nTo delete all phone numbers, select Black list → i → Delete → All → Yes → Enter \nPhone Password → f (OK).\nAccept/Reject Calls from Unknown Numbers\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Unknown → On or Off\nAccept/Reject Calls When Number is Withheld\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Withheld → On or Off\nAccept/Reject Calls from Payphones\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Payphone → On or Off\nAccept/Reject Calls When Number is Unavailable\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Unavailable → On or Off\nSave International Code\b\no 0046010\nInternational call → International code → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Enter an \ninternational code\nAdd/Change/Delete Country Number\no 日本 (Japan), 韓国 (KOR), イギリス (GBR), イタリア (ITA), \nスイス (CHE), スペイン (ESP), ドイツ (DEU), ポルトガル (PRT), \nオランダ (NLD), フランス (FRA), モナコ (MCO), アメリカ合衆国 \n(USA), スウェーデン (SWE), オーストラリア (AUS), 中国 (CHN), 香\n港 (HKG), 台湾 (TWN) \nInternational call → Country code → Add, change, or delete item\n・\n To add, press u (Add) → Select Country name field → Enter country name → In Country \ncode field, enter country code → u (Save).\n・\n To change, select country → Select Country name field → Enter country name → In Country \ncode field, enter country code → u (Save).\n・\n To delete, highlight item → i (Delete) → Yes.\nSelect Network to Access \b\no Automatic\nInternational call → Select operator → Select Auto/Manual → Select an item\n・\n When you set Manual, select a network.\nSelect Preferred Network from List\nInternational call → Select operator → Set priority → i → Insert → Network list \n→ Select a network\nAdd a New Preferred Network\nInternational call → Select operator → Set priority → i → Insert → New Network \n→ In Country code field, enter country code → In Network code field, enter Network code \n→ Select Network name field → Enter Network name → u (Save) \nSet Roaming Dial Assistant\b\no On\nInternational call → Roaming dial assistant → On or Off\n・\n If Roaming dial assistant is set to On, popup appears while dialing. If you add international \nnumber before phone number, popup does not appear.\nActivate/Cancel Offline Mode\b\no Off\nOffline → On or Off\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-10\n13\nShow/Hide Your Own Number\nCaller ID → On or Off\n・\n To check current status, select Get status.\nSet Handset to Automatically Redial Busy Numbers\b\no Off\nAuto redial → On or Off\n・\n On: Handset automatically disconnects call and redials busy numbers. Auto redial dials up to \nten times until i (Cancel) / y is pressed.\n・\n If called party uses Call Forwarding or Voicemail, call is forwarded accordingly.\nActivate/Cancel Automatic Ringer Reduction\b\no On\nRingtone reducer → On or Off\n・\n When Ringtone volume level is high, the volume level is reduced to Level 1 for the first four \nseconds, then returns to the set level.\nEnable/Disable Calling via Stereo Earphone Microphone\b\no Off\nEarphone call → On/Off → On → Call number → Select an item → Add a phone \nnumber\n・\n On: Press Stereo Earphone Microphone (optional) switch for 1 + seconds to call specified \nnumber. To change specified number, repeat setup operation, to save the new number.\nSet Clear Talk\b\no On Clear talk → On or Off\nAdjust Earpiece Volume\b\no Level 5\nHearing volume → s to adjust volume\nPhone Book Settings\nk\t\nf → Phone → Settings\nSelect Phone Book Save Location\b\no Phone\nSave to → Select an item\n・\n Always ask: Select save location each time a new entry is saved.\nChange Phone Book Preference (Phone/USIM) \b\no Phone\nChange view → Select an item\nChange Search Method\b\no ABC\nSearch method → Select an item\nSet Font Size\b\no Standard\nFont size → Select item\nCopy All Phone Book Entries & Save on Handset & USIM Card\nCopy all → Phone to USIM/USIM to Phone → Yes\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-11\n13\nMessaging Settings\nCustom Mail Address\nCustomize/Change Handset Mail Address\nu → Settings → Custom mail address → Follow onscreen instructions\n・\n Change mail account name (alphanumerics before @).\nDefault: Account name consists of random alphanumerics.\nS! Mail & SMS\nk\t\nu → Settings → Universal settings\nRequest/Cancel Delivery Report\b\no Off\nSending settings → Delivery report → On or Off\n・\n On: Receive a message confirming successful delivery of a sent message.\nQuote Text from Received Message\b\no On (Except SMS & Graphic mail) Sending settings → Reply with history → Select an item\nSelect Reply Setting\b\no Off\nSending settings → Reply settings → On or Off \n\t\nOn: Replies to sent messages are automatically addressed to \"Reply to\" address\n\t\nOff: Replies to sent messages are addressed to handset number/mail address\n・\n Set address that appears in To: field of message recipient handset.\nSet \"Reply to\" Address\nSending settings → \"Reply to\" address → Enter an item → Enter address\nChange Quick Reply Message\nSending settings → Quick reply setting → Select items → Enter message\nShow/Hide Transmission Progress Bar\b\no On\nSending settings → Sending progress → On or Off\nSet Received Message Notice Content/Hide Notice\b\no From\nReceiving settings → Message notice → View setting → Select an item\n・\n Received message notice scrolls above active function windows.\nSelect Secret Folder Message Notice Setting \b\no Show\nReceiving settings → Message notice → Secret folder → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Select an item\n・\n Not show: Incoming message notice window for messages sorted to secret folders or \nMessage notice does not appear.\nLink External Light to Incoming Feeling Mail\b\no On\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Light color → On/Off → On or Off \n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-12\n13\nLink External Light Color to Incoming Feeling Mail\no Happy/Glad: Pink, OK/Good: Green, Sad/Sorry: Blue, NG/Bad: Light \nBlue, Important/Notice: Yellow\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Light color → Light color → Select a feeling \n→ Select a color\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\nLink Vibration to Incoming Feeling Mail\b\no On\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Vibration pattern → On/Off\nSet Whether to Sound Handset When Feeling Mail Arrives\b\no Off\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Ringtone → On/Off → On or Off \nLink Ringtone to Incoming Feeling Mail\no Happy/Glad: Cheerful whistle , OK/Good: On_time, Sad/Sorry: \nRemember me, NG/Bad: Dear me, Important/Notice: Attention please\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Ringtone → Assign tone → Select a feeling \n→ Select a save location → Select a Ringtone\n・\n Press u (Play) to playback the file.\nSet Feeling Mail Ringtone Duration \b\no 5 Seconds\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Ringtone → Duration → Enter duration \n→ f (OK) \nChange Font Size\b\no Standard\nDisplay settings → Font size → Select an item\nChange Scroll Unit\b\no Single line\nDisplay settings → Scroll unit → Select an item\nChange Received Message View\b\no Folder view\nDisplay settings → Received msg. view → Select an item\nChange Sent Message View\b\no Folder view\nDisplay settings → Sent msg. view → Select an item\nSet/Cancel Auto Delete for Received Messages When Received Memory is \nFull\b\no On (Except protected) \nAuto delete → Received msg. → Select an item\nOn (Except protected): Unprotected messages are automatically deleted oldest first to make \nroom for new ones. If Auto delete is Off, memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages \nand retry.\nOn (Only read): Read messages are automatically deleted from the oldest one to make room \nfor new ones. If Auto delete is Off, memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages and \nretry.\nOff: Memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages and retry.\nSet/Cancel Auto Delete for Sent Messages When Sent Memory is Full\n\b\no On (Except protected) \nAuto delete → Sent msg. → Select an item\nOn (Except protected): Unprotected messages are automatically deleted the oldest first \nto make room for new ones. If Auto delete is Off, memory full confirmation appears. Delete \nmessages and retry.\nOff: Memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages and retry.\nSort Unregistered Mobile Address as Spam \b\no Off\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Unregistered → On\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-13\n13\nSort Message with Spam Filter\b\no Off\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Unregistered → On\n・\n To specify list, Spam filter → u (Edit) → (If address already exists in the list, i → Add \nfilter) → Sender/Sender (Partial match)/Subject → (fP.4-14 Sorting Messages c) \nAdd Address to Permitted List\b\no Off\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Permitted list → On\n・\n To specify list, Permitted list → u (Edit) → (If address already exists in the list, i → Add \nfilter) → Sender/Sender (Partial match)/Subject → (fP.4-14 Sorting Messages c).\n・\n Available only when Unregistered/Spam filter is On.\nSet Address for Report Spam\t\n\b\no stop@meiwaku.softbankmobile.co.jp\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Address for report spam \n→ Enter mail address → Yes\nSelect Save Location for Message\b\no Memory card first\nSave to → Select an item \n・\n If Always ask is selected, confirmation appears each time a message item is saved.\nS! Mail\nk\t\nu → Settings → S! Mail settings\nSet Max Creation Size\b\no 2MB\nSending options → Max creation size → Select an item \n・\n In S! Mail creation window, press i → Sending options → Max creation size → Select \nitem can change maximum size temporarily.\nSet Message Sending Priority\b\no Normal\nSending options → Priority → Select an item\nSet Picture Auto Resize\b\no 500KB\nSending options → Picture auto resize → Select item\nSet Max Receiving Size\b\no 2MB\nReceiving options → Max receiving size → 2MB/300KB\nSet S! Mail Receiving Options\b\no On (Up to 1MB) \nReceiving options → Auto receiving → Select an item\n\t\nOn (Up to 1MB): Receives maximum 1 MB automatically.\n \nOn (Up to 300KB): Receives maximum 300 KB automatically.\n\t\nOff: Mail Service Center sends S! Mail Notice; retrieve complete message.\nSet Auto Receiving Condition\b\no All messages\nReceiving options → Auto receiving conditions → All messages/Specified address\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-14\n13\nEdit Auto Receiving Condition\nReceiving options → Auto receiving conditions → Highlight Specified address → u \n(Edit) → Check item → f (OK)\n・\n If Individual address is checked, press u (Edit) → Select item → Select/Enter address/\nnumber/domain → u (OK).\nInsert/Hide Signature\b\no Off\nSignature → Auto insert → Select an item\n・\n To select Auto insert, Signature → Enter signature.\nEdit Signature\nSignature → Signature texts → Enter a signature\nSet Attached Image Appearance\b\no Normal\nPicture appearance → Select an item\nSet Attached Image Auto Playback\b\no On\nAuto play file → Picture → On or Off\nSet Attached Sound Auto Playback\b\no Off\nAuto play file → Sound → On or Off\nSMS\nk\t\nu → Settings → SMS settings\nSet Mail Service Center Message Expiry Time\b\no None\nExpiry time → Select an item\n・\n Upon expiry Mail Service Center SMS messages are automatically deleted.\nSet Message Center Number\b\no +819066519300\nMessage center → Select an item\nChange Character Code\b\no Unicode Char-code → Select an item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-15\n13\nInternet Settings\nYahoo! Keitai\nk\t\nf → Yahoo! → Browser settings\nChange Page Font Size\b\no Standard\nFont size → Select an item\nSet Encoding\b\no Auto\nEncoding → Select item\nSet Page Scroll Unit\b\no Single line\nScroll unit → Select an item\nSet Whether to Use Pointer\b\no Off\nPointer settings → On/Off → On or Off\nSet Pointer Speed\b\no Normal\nPointer settings → Speed → Select item\nShow/Hide Page Images\b\no Show images\nDownloads → Images → Select item\n・\n Select Do not show to help reduce download time.\nPlay/Mute Page Sounds\b\no Play sounds\nDownloads → Sounds → Select item\n・\n Select Do not play to help reduce download time.\nSet Save Location for Images in a Page, etc.\b\no Memory card first\nSave to → Memory card first/Phone/Always ask\n・\n To save a file to Memory Card, insert Memory Card and select Memory card first.\nDelete Cache/Cookie/Certificates\nMemory manager → Select an item → Yes\nShow/Hide Manufacture Number\b\no On\nSecurity → Manufacture number → On or Off\n・\n On: Handset automatically sends Manufacture Number to websites upon request as user ID.\nSend/Hide Referrer\b\no Send\nSecurity → Send referer → Select an item\n・\n Referrer is a link source URL information. It is sent to Web server when accessing websites.\nSelect Cookie Setting\b\no Enabled\nSecurity → Cookies → Select an item\n・\n Select Confirm to show acceptance confirmation every time before a cookie is saved.\n・\n Cookie automatically saves identification information of visitors to handset. Cookies contain \nuser information and allow sites to recognize users and track preferences.\nSelect Script Setting\b\no Ask NW access\nSecurity → Script → Select item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-16\n13\nConfirm Root Certificate\nSecurity → Root certificates → Select a certificate\n・\n View electronic certificate preinstalled on handset.\nSet Certificate Retention Period\b\no Per browsing\nSecurity → Certificate retention → Select an item\nShow/Hide Secure Prompt\b\no On\nSecurity → Secure prompt → On/Off\n・\n When opening security page, set whether to show notification.\nInitialize Browser\nInitialize browser → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n・\n Initialize browser settings or information such as Bookmarks or Saved pages.\nReset Settings\nReset settings → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\nPC Site Browser\nk\t\nf → Yahoo! → PC site browser → PC site browser settings\nChange Page Font Size\b\no Standard\nFont size → Select an item\nSet Encoding\b\no Auto\nEncoding → Select item\nSet Scroll Unit\b\no Single line\nScroll unit → Select item\nSet Whether to Use Pointer\b\no Off\nPointer settings → On/Off → On or Off\nSet Pointer Speed\b\no Normal\nPointer settings → Speed → Select item\nShow/Hide Page Navigation\b\no On\nPage navigation → On/Off\nShow/Hide Page Images\b\no Show images\nDownloads → Images → Select item\n・\n Select Do not show to help reduce download time.\nPlay/Mute Page Sounds\b\no Play sounds\nDownloads → Sounds → Select item\n・\n Select Do not play to help reduce download time.\nSet Save Location for Images in a Page, etc.\b\no Memory card first\nSave to → Memory card first/Phone/Always ask\n・\n To save a file to Memory Card, insert Memory Card and select Memory card first.\nDelete Cache/Cookie/Certificates\nMemory manager → Select an item → Yes\nDeleting RSS Feed List\nMemory manager → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-17\n13\nShow/Hide Manufacture Number\b\no On\nSecurity → Manufacture number → On or Off\n・\n On: Handset automatically sends Manufacture Number to websites upon request as user ID.\nSend/Hide Referrer\b\no Send\nSecurity → Send referer → Select an item\n・\n Referrer is a link source URL information. It is sent to Web server when accessing websites.\nSelect Cookie Setting\b\no Enabled\nSecurity → Cookies → Select an item\n・\n Select Confirm to show acceptance confirmation every time before Cookie is saved.\n・\n Cookie automatically saves identification information of visitors to handset. Cookies contain \nuser information and allow sites to recognize users and track preferences.\nSelect Script Setting\b\no On\nSecurity → Script → Select an item\nConfirm Root Certificate\nSecurity → Root certificates → Select a certificate\n・\n View electronic certificate preinstalled on handset.\nSet Certificate Retention Period\b\no Per browsing\nSecurity → Certificate retention → Select an item\nShow/Hide Secure Prompt\b\no On\nSecurity → Secure prompt → On/Off\n・\n When opening security page, set whether to show notification.\nShow/Hide Warning\b\no On Warning messages → On or Off\n・\n Show/hide PC Site Browser activation, or Yahoo! Keitai/PC Site Browser switching warning.\nInitialize Browser\nInitialize browser → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n・\n Initialize browser settings or information such as Bookmarks or Saved pages.\nReset Settings\nReset settings → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-18\n13\nCamera Settings\nPhoto\nk\t\n j → i → \n → Settings\nSelect Quality\b\no Superfine\nQuality → Select an item\nSet ISO\b\no Auto\nISO → Select an item\nSet Exposure Metering\b\no Center-weight\nExposure metering → Select an item\nSelect Effect\b\no None\nEffect → Select item\nActivate/Cancel Auto Save\b\no On (Preview manual) \nSetup → Auto save → On (Preview Off)/On (Preview 2 sec)/On (Preview manual)/\nOff\n・\n On (Preview Off): Image is automatically saved. After saving, handset returns to Viewfinder \nwithout showing preview.\n・\n On (Preview 2 sec): Image is automatically saved. After saving, preview appears for two \nseconds, and handset returns to Viewfinder.\n・\n On (Preview manual): After capturing, image is automatically saved and preview appears.\n・\n Off: Select save or cancel the image. To redo, press c. To save, press f (Save).\nSet Save Location When Memory Card is Inserted\n\b\no Memory card first\nSetup → Save to → Select an item\n・\n This setting is active with Memory Card inserted.\n・\n If Memory Card is not inserted, images are automatically saved to Phone.\nAdjust Flicker\b\no Auto\nSetup → Flicker adjustment → Auto/50Hz (East Japan)/50Hz (West Japan) \nShow/Hide Guideline\b\no Off\nSetup → Guideline → On or Off\nSet Face Link Display\b\no Off\nSetup → Face link display → On or Off\n・\n When you set this On, after the face you captured is recognized, Face Link appears.\nSet Shutter Sound\b\no Pattern1 Setup → Shutter sound → Select an item\nSet Timer Sound\b\no Pattern1 Setup → Timer sound → Select an item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-19\n13\nVideo\nk\t\nj (1+ seconds) → Video camera → i → \n → Settings\nSelect Quality\b\no Superfine\nQuality → Select an item\nSet Effect\b\no None\nEffect → Select item\nSet Sound Recording\b\no On\nSound recording → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Auto Save\b\no On\nSetup → Auto save → On or Off\nSet Save Location\b\no Memory card first\nSetup → Save to → Select item\n・\n To save a file to Memory Card, insert Memory Card.\nShow/Hide Guideline\b\no Off\nSetup → Guideline → On or Off\nAdjust Flicker\b\no Auto\nSetup → Flicker adjustment → Auto/50Hz (East Japan)/50Hz (West Japan) \nSet Shutter Sound\b\no Pattern1 Setup → Shutter sound → Select an item\nSet Timer Sound\b\no Pattern1 Setup → Timer sound → Select an item\nMedia Player Settings\nMusic\nk\t\nf → Media → Settings → Music settings\nSet Repeat Mode\b\no All\nRepeat mode → Select an item\n・\n Play a single track and all music/all files in playlist repeatedly.\nSet Shuffle\b\no Off\nShuffle → On or Off\n.\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-20\n13\nMovie\nk\t\nf → Media → Settings → Movie settings\nSet Repeat Mode\b\no All\nRepeat mode → Select an item\n・\n Play a single file repeatedly, all movies, or all files in playlist repeatedly.\nSet Shuffle\b\no Off\nShuffle → On or Off\nSet Backlight\b\no Always on\nBacklight → Select an item\nSet Portrait Style\b\no 240 * 180\nDisplay → Portrait style → Select an item\nSet Display for Activating Movie\b\no Landscape\nDisplay → First view → Select an item\nShow/Hide Movie Preview\b\no On\nDisplay → Preview → On or Off\nAccess/Ignore Linked Information\b\no On Web link → On or Off\n・\n On: After playing a file with linked info, access confirmation appears.\nEntertainment Settings\nS! Information Channel\nk\t\nf → Entertainment → S! Information Channel/Weather → Weather Indicator → Settings\nSet Weather Indicator Display Settings\b\no On\nDisplay setting → On or Off\nSet Weather Indicator Update Notification\b\no On\nMissed event setting → On or Off\nSet Weather Indicator Automatic Update\b\no On\nAuto update → On or Off → Yes as required\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-21\n13\nSecurity Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Security\nActivate/Cancel Phone Lock\b\no Off\nPhone lock → On or Off → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \nActivate/Cancel Password Lock\b\no Off\nPassword lock → On → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \nChange Phone Password\b\no 9999 Change password → Enter current password → f (OK) → Enter new password → f (OK) \n→ Enter new password again → f (OK) \nActivate/Cancel Function Lock\b\no All unlocked\nFunction lock → Check an item → u (Save) → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) \nActivate/Cancel Secret Mode\b\no Hide\nSecret mode → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Select an item\nActivate/Cancel USIM Lock \b\no Off\nUSIM lock → On or Off → Enter USIM Password (four- to eight-digit) → f (OK) → Enter \nUSIM Password again as required → f (OK) \nActivate/Cancel PIN Certification\b\no Off\nPIN certification → On or Off → Enter PIN → f (OK) \nChange PIN\nChange PIN → Enter current PIN → f (OK) → Enter new PIN → f (OK) → Enter new \nPIN again → f (OK)\n・\n To change PIN code, set PIN certification to On.\nChange PIN2\nChange PIN2 → Enter current PIN2 → f (OK) → Enter new PIN2 → f (OK) → Enter \nnew PIN2 again → f (OK) \nSet Secret Mode on Sub-folder in Data Folder\b\no Hide\nSecret data folder → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Select item\nDelete Phone Book Entries, Messages, etc.\nReset → All reset → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\nRestore Settings to Default Values\nReset → Reset settings → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\nSet Mobile Tracker\b\no Off\nMobile tracker → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Activation → On → Recipients \n→ Select To field → Phonebook/Direct input → Search and select 